<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/00683550-a89a-4865-8633-222f7600d5e6> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#resultsIn> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/6db03a02-b135-48eb-b409-f484614cc58a> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/00683550-a89a-4865-8633-222f7600d5e6> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#weighs> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Alternative/73f4c2dc-b853-4a94-8db2-56ac1828755b> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/00683550-a89a-4865-8633-222f7600d5e6> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#weighs> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Alternative/eec8eb3f-b2d4-45ed-9351-3048d0831dd1> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/00683550-a89a-4865-8633-222f7600d5e6> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#weighs> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Alternative/f8becc95-31dc-43f9-a3ea-ac9f806b976c> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/017b993e-e549-408f-8adc-0a950d76ea65> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#ArchitecturalDecision> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/017b993e-e549-408f-8adc-0a950d76ea65> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Role inclusions are matched through the told closure, not materialized" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/017b993e-e549-408f-8adc-0a950d76ea65> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/017b993e-e549-408f-8adc-0a950d76ea65> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "HOWL no longer has a role-hierarchy rule. R(r) is read through the told role hierarchy: an edge is stored under the role it was derived with, and (X,Y) ∈ R(s) whenever it is stored under some e with s ∈ sup*(e). This is ELK's treatment (Kazakov, Krötzsch & Simančík, The Incredible ELK). Before, CR6 ((X,Y) ∈ R(r), r ⊑ s ⟹ (X,Y) ∈ R(s), published CR10) copied every edge under each super-role. Those copies were about 1.6M of EL-GALEN's 1.8M new edges, each queued, joined and committed.\n\n**How it works (M1 slice 6b D2).**\n- **The closure.** `build-rule-index` (premise.slop) computes a `RoleClosure`: sup*(r) for every role some axiom mentions, by breadth-first walk with a visited set (equivalent properties make the hierarchy cyclic), and its inverse sub*. A role no axiom mentions has no entry and needs none.\n- **The dispatcher applies it (el.slop).** An arriving edge under e is offered to the CR4/CR7 axioms of every r ∈ sup*(e), with r as the rule's role. When a rule walks a stored side (CR4 on a new subsumer walks preds; CR7 walks the other leg), it is handed the axiom rewritten to name each e ∈ sub*(walked role).\n- **The rule functions and their proved contracts are unchanged.** Every rule still sees one concrete role. CR6 and its two proved properties are deleted, leaving five proved loop-free rules and 11 properties; `make verify` proves 35 functions.\n- **Transitivity is not in the closure.** It is the chain r ∘ r ⊑ r, applied by CR7 with both legs matched through sup*.\n\n**Why the subsumptions are unchanged.** Materializing added exactly the edges (X,Y):s for s ∈ sup*(e), and every reader of R(s) (CR4, CR7; CR5 ignores roles) now sees them through the closure.\n\n**Evidence.**\n- On all 79 fixtures and the 4 corpora, every report line except `rounds` is byte-identical to the CR6 engine's. Rounds changed on 3 fixtures (5→4, 5→4, 8→7) and on EL-GALEN (31→26).\n- `diff-corpus` is clean, with oracle-entailments and subsumptions (499,983 on EL-GALEN) unchanged.\n- The new hazards/role-hierarchy-deep.ttl agrees with both HermiT and ELK.\n- Six mutations were each seen red: a one-level closure, no sub* walk for CR4-on-subsumer, CR7 legs matched by exact role (each direction), a reference dispatcher without the closure, and no visited set (hangs).\n\nCodex review found no entailment loss. Its one finding was fixed: the reference dispatcher shared the indexed one's sub* helpers, so a shared mistake would pass the differential. The reference now has its own fixpoint closure and walks the stored roles testing sup* membership." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/017b993e-e549-408f-8adc-0a950d76ea65> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/017b993e-e549-408f-8adc-0a950d76ea65> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-09-29T08:16:24.919808Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
