<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/017b993e-e549-408f-8adc-0a950d76ea65> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#weighs> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Alternative/fa7213b8-6aad-491b-afd8-4d17b2f1d903> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/0394c537-72e1-4b00-8079-7d30846b47fa> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#ArchitecturalDecision> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/0394c537-72e1-4b00-8079-7d30846b47fa> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "The §12 benchmark times certified inputs and answers over a conservative classification window" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/0394c537-72e1-4b00-8079-7d30846b47fa> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/0394c537-72e1-4b00-8079-7d30846b47fa> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "`make bench` (bench/bench.py, results in bench/results.txt) implements SPEC §12's protocol. It times HOWL's classification as `prepare_ms + reason_ms` and the oracle's as reasoner creation + consistency check + `precomputeInferences`. It takes the median of 5 runs after 1 warm-up, at W = 4 for HOWL and for ELK (set in code and read back). It gates only ELK-routed entries, at 5x.\n\n**Classification window.**\n- **The oracle's window.** ELK 0.6.0 loads and indexes its axioms lazily, at the first query (`isConsistent`), and HermiT does so in its constructor. So both oracles do their indexing inside their window.\n- **HOWL's window.** It includes decode (RDF triples → axioms), which the oracle does in its OWL API parse.\n- **Why.** The comparison therefore charges HOWL for more, never less. A gate may not be more permissive than the proof it cites.\n\n**Routing.** The bench uses the oracle `make diff-corpus` recorded in corpus/corpus-differential.txt:\n- ELK for GO and EL-GALEN, which are gated;\n- HermiT for the range-bearing RO and OBI, which are reported only, since §12 sets no threshold against a complete oracle.\n\n**Certified input, certified answer.** A timing is always of the exact input and answer the differential certified clean. Before timing, each file must pass diff-corpus's own content check (`project.check_graph`: ground sha, blank-node count and structure). The projection pins must equal the differential's recorded `ground`/`bnodes`. Then:\n- every HOWL run's report must hash to `howl-report`, with `termination fixpoint` and `omitted 0`;\n- every oracle run's entailment lines must hash to `oracle-entailments`;\n- the input and the binary must not change during the run.\n\n**Verdicts.** The verdict is computed from the medians as written, so `run` and `check` judge the same number.\n\n**Runs.** HOWL's runs are separate processes. The oracle's share one JIT-warm JVM, which favours the oracle. The load average is recorded at the start and end.\n\n**Evidence.**\n- Mutation checks were refused end to end: a different answer pin, a doctored input with the same answer, a capped run, and a wrong oracle pin.\n- Codex review findings (input unpinned, rounding at the threshold, run sequence) were all fixed; 22 unit tests." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/0394c537-72e1-4b00-8079-7d30846b47fa> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "superseded" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
