<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/072fdfe9-1269-4159-9219-9283a34642ad> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Saturation runs over nodes renamed to dense fresh ids at its boundary" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/072fdfe9-1269-4159-9219-9283a34642ad> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/072fdfe9-1269-4159-9219-9283a34642ad> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "`normalize-input` (M1 slice 6b C2) renames every Node and RoleId that saturation will see to `(fresh-node k)`/`(fresh-role k)` through one `Names` table (types.slop). That covers the signature, the normal form, the asserted edges, the seeds and the asserted subjects. Extraction maps them back before it tests for classes or sorts.\n\n**Why.** A class node, individual node or named role is compared and hashed as its whole IRI; a fresh one as an Int. Generated Node/RoleId hash+eq was ~28% of EL-GALEN's reasoning work.\n\n**Why it is sound.** Nothing in the rules, the premise index or the driver reads a node's tag or IRI, only equality. So they run unchanged, and so does every proved `@property`. There are two exceptions and one ordering constraint:\n- ⊤ and ⊥ are never renamed, because the rules build them as constants.\n- Punned class and individual names stay distinct, because the table is keyed by the whole node.\n- `signature-nodes` runs on the original output first: it mints fresh ids that would collide with renamed ones.\n\n**Carriers.** `Prepared.names` and `Outcome.names`. `entails-sub` maps the caller's original nodes forward. An unknown fresh node under a non-empty table answers false rather than reading the context of whatever node now holds that id; this was the Codex review's one finding.\n\n**Result.** Reports are unchanged: goldens, the corpus report hashes, and determinism across 2,016 comparisons. Reasoning is ~20% faster side by side.\n\n| Entry | C1 | C2 |\n|---|---|---|\n| GO | 5.89× | 5.62× |\n| EL-GALEN | 7.74× | 6.43× |\n\nThe C was generated from slop origin/main 9d38064.\n\n**Verification.**\n- Mutations, each seen red: taxonomy not mapped back; seeds installed un-renamed; ⊤ renamed; `entails-sub` without the forward map.\n- `test-names-round-trip` covers inversion, ⊤ and ⊥, punning, and the identity table." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/072fdfe9-1269-4159-9219-9283a34642ad> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
