<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/0a305284-0b59-47e0-ba53-e00b48012cba> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#ArchitecturalDecision> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/0a305284-0b59-47e0-ba53-e00b48012cba> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "The front end frees its arenas as each phase ends; survivors own their strings" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/0a305284-0b59-47e0-ba53-e00b48012cba> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/0a305284-0b59-47e0-ba53-e00b48012cba> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "HOWL no longer runs parse through report in one run-long arena. Each front-end phase's intermediates live in a scratch arena freed when the phase ends, and the few products that outlive the front end are built in the result arena and own their strings (memory_work, commits 4eb41a8 and 103e45d).\n\n**The frees:**\n- Stage 0 and `decode-axioms` each build their TermStore (and stage 0 its header sets) in a scratch arena freed before returning. The store keeps terms by value, with parser-owned strings, and queries copy terms out, so nothing decoded points into it.\n- `prepare-decoded` runs the gate and the normalizer in a scratch arena freed before returning. Names, the renamed axioms and signature, the saturation and the index are built in the result arena.\n- The library's `prepare` decodes into its own arena and frees it. The CLI parses and decodes into a `front` arena that `prepare-from` frees before reasoning.\n\n**What survives, and is copied:**\n- **Names:** `intern-node` / `intern-role` copy the original IRI on first sight; ⊤ and ⊥ are the static constants.\n- **The omissions:** `copy-omissions`, also used for the `refused` fault.\n- **A decode fault's message:** `copy-fault`.\n\nNothing else crosses the boundary: the index and the saturation hold renamed Ints. A Prepared or Outcome therefore owns every string it holds, and a port caller's triples may be dropped as soon as `prepare` returns.\n\n**The rule that shapes the code.** A slop collection grows in whatever arena its push/put site names `arena` (lexically), not the arena it was created in. So survivors are built only by calls handed the result arena, and scratch structures only by calls handed the scratch arena.\n\n**Step A cut waste outright:**\n- the CLI's full copy of the triple list;\n- rendered text for ~0.8M inert annotation axioms, which are now a payload-less `ra-annotation`, counted in `Stage1.inert` rather than kept;\n- the gate's second rendering of every accepted axiom, now rendered only for an undeclared entity.\n\n**Safety net.** `make golden-asan` builds the CLI under ASan and runs `golden` over every fixture plus RO and OBI. A memory error exits 99." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/0a305284-0b59-47e0-ba53-e00b48012cba> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
