<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/0a305284-0b59-47e0-ba53-e00b48012cba> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#resultsIn> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/6777b52b-af7e-41e8-a762-7cdd3c04249f> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/0a305284-0b59-47e0-ba53-e00b48012cba> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#weighs> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Alternative/528938d3-16e7-469d-89a5-092a07d1b221> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/0a305284-0b59-47e0-ba53-e00b48012cba> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#weighs> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Alternative/6842dcce-97c7-4272-8a9b-14c08f2a9d42> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/0a305284-0b59-47e0-ba53-e00b48012cba> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#weighs> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Alternative/abf9658d-21e4-4c04-964b-3082252c98be> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/0c2bf0d7-3589-44d6-908f-da3eed5a4f57> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#ArchitecturalDecision> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/0c2bf0d7-3589-44d6-908f-da3eed5a4f57> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "A saturation round's queues live in generation arenas freed a round later" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/0c2bf0d7-3589-44d6-908f-da3eed5a4f57> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/0c2bf0d7-3589-44d6-908f-da3eed5a4f57> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Each saturation round allocates its queues and next frontier in a GENERATION of arenas, freed once the round after it has committed (memory_work commit 4db10d3). Before, every round's queues, the committers' queue tables and the frontier maps went into the run arena and the long-lived commit arenas, and the whole history of Δ stayed resident until exit.\n\n**How it works:**\n- **Two arenas per committer.** `commit-entry` takes two, both the committer's own: the store grows in its commit arena `ca`, through `commit-sub`, `commit-succ` and `commit-pred`, and the round's queues grow in `arena`, a queue arena.\n- **One generation per round.** `advance-round` creates it: one arena for the queue and frontier maps (at W = 1 this is also the committer's queue arena), plus one per committer at W > 1, since an arena is not thread-safe.\n- **Arena roles in `commit-round`.** Its `arena` is the generation arena, and the run arena arrives as `run` for `partition-round`'s context creation. The `record-new` stays last, so the proved round-count `@post`s still discharge.\n- **The loop frees the old generation.** `saturate` keeps the previous generation's arena list, which lives in the run arena so freeing never reads freed memory, and frees it after each `advance-round`.\n- **What is never freed.** Δ₀'s queues live in the run arena; the last generation stays with the result.\n\nEach committer still owns its arenas and the join only reads, so determinism (§6.8) and context independence (§6.6) are unchanged. Reports are byte-identical, and TSan and determinism are clean." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/0c2bf0d7-3589-44d6-908f-da3eed5a4f57> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/0c2bf0d7-3589-44d6-908f-da3eed5a4f57> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-09-29T17:14:04.784627Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/0c2bf0d7-3589-44d6-908f-da3eed5a4f57> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "A saturation round's queues live in generation arenas freed a round later" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/0c2bf0d7-3589-44d6-908f-da3eed5a4f57> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#isConstrainedBy> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/007e982c-4936-4607-8bda-33451359f836> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/0c2bf0d7-3589-44d6-908f-da3eed5a4f57> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#resultsIn> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/79fd3f3f-2fb1-4b26-bef7-44a641e56d52> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/17beb51b-607b-4ff3-99de-b2afbb9dc801> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#ArchitecturalDecision> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/17beb51b-607b-4ff3-99de-b2afbb9dc801> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "HOWL and GROWL compose through RDF, never shared state" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/17beb51b-607b-4ff3-99de-b2afbb9dc801> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/17beb51b-607b-4ff3-99de-b2afbb9dc801> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "The two engines never touch each other's memory. HOWL classifies and emits inferred subClassOf axioms as RDF; GROWL materializes and enriches over the enlarged schema. Everything crossing the boundary is RDF — the first two pipeline stages (parse, RDF-to-axiom) and the last (emit Turtle) ARE the composition seam.\n\nWhy: it keeps GROWL stable and production-safe while HOWL evolves, and it lets either engine run standalone. The two are complementary rather than competing — GROWL materializes OWL 2 RL (sound, deliberately incomplete for OWL-DL, best at enrichment and bulk ABox work), HOWL classifies a named description logic (sound AND complete for its fragment, best at defined-class subsumption and coherence of definitions and mappings).\n\nCorollary on sequencing: do not pre-refactor GROWL. Leaving it untouched is deliberate — the first move WHEN HOWL WORK STARTS is to lift the shared substrate (Turtle parse/serialize, Term/IRI/blank-node interning, IndexedGraph and arena utilities, the fixpoint control skeleton, worker pool and config plumbing) into a common library. Not copy-paste, and not a speculative refactor now.\n\nThe relationship is not purely one-directional, though. The consumer's pipeline runs an agreement stage that cross-checks the TBox and ABox engines on a deterministic probe set IN THE EL-INTERSECT-RL ENTAILMENT OVERLAP, where disagreement is an ENGINE FAULT and is never resolved by preferring one engine. So HOWL and GROWL are also independent oracles checked against each other in production: differential testing stops being a CI activity and becomes a live mechanism, and agreement with GROWL on the overlap becomes a standing correctness obligation.\n\nEvidence: SPEC.md §1 (the complementary-services table), §8.1 (shared vs. new), §8.2 (composition), §8.3 (do not pre-refactor), §8.4 (dual-engine cross-check), §10 test 19." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/17beb51b-607b-4ff3-99de-b2afbb9dc801> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
