<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/1db0fb50-6331-4521-9a80-c7920f3db916> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#ArchitecturalDecision> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/1db0fb50-6331-4521-9a80-c7920f3db916> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "el++ rounds are barrier rounds; phases G and W derive in parallel" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/1db0fb50-6331-4521-9a80-c7920f3db916> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/1db0fb50-6331-4521-9a80-c7920f3db916> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "el++'s `ksc-round` uses el's barrier model (SPEC §6.8), which is exactly §5.4's definition of a round. It replaces commit-on-derive.\n\n**How a round runs:**\n- `Sₙ` is frozen at the round's start, `Δₙ` included.\n- `derive-round` splits `Δₙ` into contiguous chunks, one per worker (up to `--workers`).\n- Each `derive-chunk` derives against the frozen store and keeps, as 16-byte CFacts in its own arena, the conclusions `store-holds` says the store and base lack.\n- A serial commit walks the chunks in order. `commit-coded` checks only the run's `seen`, which is sound because the base is frozen for the whole run and the worker already filtered against `Sₙ`. It then files the fact and pushes it to `Δₙ₊₁`, stopping at the first ⊥ under stop-at-bottom.\n\n**Why every report is W-independent:**\n- A derivation reads only the frozen store.\n- The commit sees `Δₙ`'s order at every W.\n- So answers, rounds, counts and capped runs are identical at every worker count.\n\n**Scope.** Phases G and W use `config.worker-count`. Phase Q's class runs use 1 worker each, since they are already parallel across classes.\n\n**Rounds.** Counts shift slightly from the commit-on-derive engine (EL-GALEN 27 → 28); answers do not change." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/1db0fb50-6331-4521-9a80-c7920f3db916> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/1db0fb50-6331-4521-9a80-c7920f3db916> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-10-02T22:31:33.506239Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
