<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/355c704f-3a87-4ed5-8ef3-907994d30ffe> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Profile ladder: el, el++, horn-sriq, sriq; default el" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/355c704f-3a87-4ed5-8ef3-907994d30ffe> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/355c704f-3a87-4ed5-8ef3-907994d30ffe> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "HOWL's selectable profiles are one rung per named logic. The default on every surface (CLI, C, Rust, port) is `explicit el`; `auto` is an opt-in. SPEC §5 and §5.1 define the ladder.\n\n| Rung | Logic | Worst case | Calculus | Status |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `el` | ELH⊥R+ + domain/range + ABox | PTIME | BBL05/BBL08, §5.3 | built |\n| `el++` | OWL 2 EL object fragment | PTIME | KKS12 ELO | planned |\n| `horn-sriq` (v1) | Horn-SRIQ | ExpTime | Kaz09 + chain elimination, or Bate+18 Horn slice | M5 |\n| `sriq` (v2) | SRIQ object fragment | 2ExpTime | Bate+18 | not scheduled |\n\n**Why these rungs:**\n- **Horn-SRIQ contains v0, Horn-SHIQ does not.** Horn-SHIQ has no chains, and the gate enforces regularity. It also removes the chain-plus-inverse case, RO and CCO among them, that was inside no rung. `el++` is the only rung left incomparable.\n- **SRIQ, not SROIQ, at the top.** The census (2026-09-30) shows the BFO family needs no nominals and no counting beyond ≤1:\n  - BFO-core is SHIF, non-Horn only through 22 unions.\n  - CCO is SRIF(D), non-Horn only through 29 unions.\n  - RO is SROIF(D) plus SWRL; its one nominal is an IAO metadata class.\n  - Functionality combined with disjunction already needs equality, so SRIQ is the least logic that is complete for BFO, CCO and RO.\n  - Full SROIQ (TGH21, Sequoia) needs the nominal Nom rule and exponential chain elimination, and no consequence-based calculus handles datatypes.\n- **`el` by default.** HOWL is a runtime system:\n  - `el` is PTIME, and adding any one of inverses, ∀, functionality, ≥2 or disjunction makes the logic ExpTime-complete (BBL05 Thms 6-11, BBL08 Thm 3, KRH13).\n  - Under an `auto` default, one added inverse would move every run into an ExpTime calculus.\n  - A default run's theory never changes under an upgrade.\n- **Explicit requests are exact.** One is honoured exactly or refused as `Fault::unavailable` (CLI exit 3), never run as another rung.\n- **The report states the profile.** Header `howl-report 2`, then `profile el`.\n\n**Code:**\n- `src/select.slop`: `select-profile`, `profile-implemented`, `profile-name`, `parse-profile`, each with pinned posts.\n- `src/howl.slop`: `prepare-decoded` resolves the profile before the gate; `prepare-in-profile` is where a second rung dispatches.\n- `default-config` sets `explicit profile-el`.\n- `rust/src/lib.rs`: `Profile`, `ProfileSelection` and `Config.selection`." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
