<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/3e6b52c2-31c1-42a7-bd3d-670739a577a9> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#ArchitecturalDecision> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/3e6b52c2-31c1-42a7-bd3d-670739a577a9> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Dispatch does each join once, from its cheaper side" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/3e6b52c2-31c1-42a7-bd3d-670739a577a9> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/3e6b52c2-31c1-42a7-bd3d-670739a577a9> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "M1 slice 6b step A removed three kinds of redundant work from saturation, without changing a single report: goldens are byte-identical, round counts included, and the RO/OBI/GO/EL-GALEN report hashes are unchanged.\n\n1. **CR6 fires from the successor half only.** `cr-role-incl-on-pred` is deleted, and both dispatchers are updated. CR6's premise is one edge plus an axiom, not a join, so one delivery of the edge suffices. The driver delivers both halves of every edge in the same round: `admit-edge` writes both, `round-commit` queues both, and `install-seeds` installs both. A handler on the predecessor half re-derived every super-role edge, 3.2M redundant messages on EL-GALEN.\n2. **`admit` handles a logical edge once, through its successor half.** `derived-pred` is a documented no-op. Every predecessor half on the admit path arrives with its successor sibling in the same rule output, because `emit-edge` is its only constructor and seeds bypass `admit`.\n3. **CR2, and CR4's on-edge trigger, walk the smaller side of their join.** This is ELK's lazy set intersection. premise.slop's two-level `Partners` buckets make it possible: `and-by-pair` maps a conjunct to its partner conjuncts, and `lhs-by-role` maps a role to its fillers, each with a count of inner keys.\n   - The dispatcher compares that count with |S(X)| (`subsumer-count`, a single `c-inline` read of `->len` until slop has `set-len`).\n   - It walks the smaller side and probes the other.\n   - Each surviving axiom still goes through the unchanged, proved rule function.\n\n**Measured call counts (single-threaded):**\n\n| Measure | EL-GALEN | GO |\n|---|---|---|\n| CR2 calls | 14.9M → 488k | 77.2M → 131k |\n| CR4 on-edge calls | 27.8M → 579k | 1.48M → 428k |\n| Edge admits | 7.71M → 2.24M | 0.97M → 0.44M |\n\nEvery CR2 and CR4 call now produces a conclusion. EL-GALEN's single-threaded reasoning samples halved.\n\n**Verification:**\n- **Gates:** every gate passes. `verify` proves 36 functions (six loop-free rules, 13 faithfulness properties).\n- **Mutations:** four were each seen red: CR6 dropped; CR2's S(X)-walk with the wrong key; CR2's partner-walk inverted; CR4's S(Y)-walk with the wrong key.\n- **Coverage gaps the mutations exposed:**\n  - At first only the corpus goldens caught three of the four mutations.\n  - No fixture entered the context-side branch of the smaller-side choice, so hazards/smaller-side-join.ttl was added.\n  - No unit test had CR6 act on an actual edge, so the subproperty-existential probe joined the dispatch differential and got its own test.\n\n  Both gaps are now closed at unit level.\n- **Codex review:** one comment correction, no findings." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
