<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/423087e8-98fd-41cf-921d-6509e8b81a99> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#ArchitecturalDecision> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/423087e8-98fd-41cf-921d-6509e8b81a99> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "The decoded document is copied out, and the encoded input freed, before the gate" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/423087e8-98fd-41cf-921d-6509e8b81a99> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/423087e8-98fd-41cf-921d-6509e8b81a99> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "After decode, the Decoded (axioms, signature, omissions) is deep-copied into its own arena and the encoded input's arena (dictionary, id triples, stage-0 output, decode's stores; ~500 MB on GO) is freed before the gate and normalizer run. Before, that arena was held through the whole of prepare and set GO's peak (913 MB). Extends AD 0a305284 (front-end phases free their arenas as they end).\n\n**How:** owl2.slop gains copy-concept / copy-raw-axiom / copy-axioms / copy-signature, with NO catch-all arm, so a new RawAxiom or RawConcept variant fails the build until it is copied. normalize.slop gains copy-decoded; howl.slop gains own-decoded (the copy, for ok and error) and decode-owned (library prepare: decode in its own arena, copy, free); the CLI's decode-held does the same for the streamed Encoded, and prepare-from frees the held copy. IRI strings are copied per occurrence (about 15 MB on GO), leaving the dictionary's literal strings behind.\n\n**Contracts:** copy-axioms proves `(list-len $result) == (list-len xs)` through a counted while with `@loop-invariant {(list-len out) == i}`; copy-decoded carries it (the callee must be let-bound: slop verify does not assume a callee's @post for a call nested inside record-new). This is a COUNT, not identity (Codex review): that each copied axiom is the same one is held by goldens and corpus hashes. The lifetime - nothing in the copy points into the freed arena - is out of the verifier's reach and held by golden-asan: leaving rc-name's IRI uncopied fails with heap-use-after-free in signature_has_class. verify 35 -> 38 verified, 0 failed, 1 unknown." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
