<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/42c907c9-7083-42d8-b53e-0daff17089d8> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#ArchitecturalDecision> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/42c907c9-7083-42d8-b53e-0daff17089d8> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "el++ calculus is Krötzsch's Ksc, with sharing by monotonicity" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/42c907c9-7083-42d8-b53e-0daff17089d8> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/42c907c9-7083-42d8-b53e-0daff17089d8> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "The `el++` rung implements Krötzsch's materialisation calculus Ksc (KIT TR 3005, 2010, Theorem 2: sound and complete for classification of SROEL(⊓,×)). It is the one published proof covering nominals together with ⊥, role hierarchies, chains with the OWL 2 EL range restriction, ranges and Self.\n\nHOWL changes Ksc's representation in two ways, both proved in SPEC §5.4:\n- **K2, sharing by monotonicity.** G, the closure of Kinst, is computed once. Each input class q then runs from `G ∪ {inst(q,q)}`, storing only facts not already in G, and its store is discarded once its answers are taken. By Datalog monotonicity and idempotence this equals Ksc's facts under q, so no new completeness proof is needed.\n- **K3, rule (4) as a flag.** ⊥ under q may arise at any element. Inconsistency is `unsat(owl:Thing)`, not \"⊥ in G\", which misses `⊤ ⊑ ⊥` when there are no individuals.\n\n**Translation (K0, K1):**\n- Ranges are native products, `R ⊑ ⊤×D`.\n- Domains are `∃R.⊤ ⊑ C`, not products, so `ran(R)` gains no ⊤ and chains are not refused.\n- `ReflexiveObjectProperty(R)` becomes `⊤ ⊑ ∃S_R.Self` and `S_R ⊑ R`, with `S_R` fresh and simple.\n- `owl:bottomObjectProperty` becomes `∃N.⊤ ⊑ ⊥`.\n- Inclusions into `owl:topObjectProperty` are dropped as tautologies.\n- Rules (19)–(22) are not implemented; their EDB predicates are always empty.\n\n**Engine:** new and separate from `el`'s. It runs phase G, then a parallel phase Q across classes, with a per-q overlay store. `rounds` = `rounds(G)` + the most rounds any single q took.\n\n**Registration:** `BoundedDl`, because EL++ includes concrete domains.\n\n**Review:** Codex adversarial review signed off after three textual fixes. The project owner approved §5.4 on 2026-09-30.\n\nEvidence: SPEC.md §5.4; TR 3005 Definition 1, Figs. 1–3, Proposition 1, Theorems 1–2; KKS12 Theorem 4 (ELO only)." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
