<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/465af4c0-7d7d-4f83-82cb-a398f7531106> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#ArchitecturalDecision> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/465af4c0-7d7d-4f83-82cb-a398f7531106> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Spec SPEC.md §5.4 (el++ calculus) approved for implementation" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/465af4c0-7d7d-4f83-82cb-a398f7531106> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/465af4c0-7d7d-4f83-82cb-a398f7531106> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "James Adam approved SPEC.md §5.4, \"The el++ calculus\", for implementation on 2026-09-30. §5.4 was added in PR #8 (merged as 13f4ff0), after SPEC.md's whole-document approval of 2026-08-17 (AD 59735b43). So this is the re-approval of that revision: it mints only what §5.4 states. The owner reviewed K2 and K3 directly. Codex's adversarial review signed off after three textual fixes.\n\nspec-approval: /Users/jcadam/code/howl/SPEC.md §5.4 (el++ calculus, 2026-09-30 revision)\n\nMinted from §5.4:\n- Requirement — Complete classification for the OWL 2 EL object fragment — Requirement/cb02e954-4f94-40e8-aff3-b47b499af95e\n- Constraint — No el++ rule is left owed — Constraint/01c06881-923f-455c-b121-e25becece9af\n- ArchitecturalDecision — el++ calculus is Krötzsch's Ksc, with sharing by monotonicity — ArchitecturalDecision/42c907c9-7083-42d8-b53e-0daff17089d8 (5 Alternatives, 4 Consequences)\n\nRecorded alongside, from the approved plan rather than mined from the spec:\n- Consequence — The ladder's el++ citation is corrected from KKS12 to Krötzsch TR 3005 — Consequence/b3fee881-1bf3-40bf-9de9-4f5d2842c6ff\n- Lesson — Check a cited completeness result: its later literature, and its logic — Lesson/3a45b0a7-cf28-45d8-abc4-08494d91b064 (supersedes Lesson/54506027, edges re-asserted)\n\nReused rather than re-minted:\n- Constraint/f8ee2abd (construct-by-construct claims; covers the BoundedDl registration);\n- Constraint/ae25e3d4 (a gate may not exceed its cited proof);\n- Constraint/793f66a9 (the v0 language el++ extends; constrains AD 42c907c9)." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/465af4c0-7d7d-4f83-82cb-a398f7531106> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/465af4c0-7d7d-4f83-82cb-a398f7531106> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-10-01T02:56:24.082857Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/465af4c0-7d7d-4f83-82cb-a398f7531106> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Spec SPEC.md §5.4 (el++ calculus) approved for implementation" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/465af4c0-7d7d-4f83-82cb-a398f7531106> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#isMotivatedBy> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Requirement/cb02e954-4f94-40e8-aff3-b47b499af95e> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/48b331ef-b073-490b-9785-e0afda7485d7> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#ArchitecturalDecision> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/48b331ef-b073-490b-9785-e0afda7485d7> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "The round-join runs on worker threads over a split of the frontier; deltas merge by set union, then commit" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/48b331ef-b073-490b-9785-e0afda7485d7> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/48b331ef-b073-490b-9785-e0afda7485d7> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "At `worker-count` W > 1, `advance-round` (src/saturate.slop `parallel-join`) runs the round in four steps:\n1. **Split.** The frontier `active` is split into up to W contiguous shares.\n2. **Join.** One thread per share (SLOP `thread` `spawn`/`join`) runs `round-join-part`, which is `round-join` over its share. Each worker writes only its own arena (`arena-new`) and its own `RoundDelta`; the store and the premise index are frozen and only read.\n3. **Merge.** After every `join`, the coordinator merges the deltas by set union (`merge-delta`) in fixed worker order, into its own scratch arena.\n4. **Commit and free.** The unchanged `round-commit` commits, and the worker arenas are freed.\n\nAt W = 1 the path is exactly the previous one. The default stays 4, so every test and the port run the parallel path. The CLI's `--workers N` (1..64, refused outside, never clamped) sets it. It appears nowhere in the report or the fingerprint.\n\n**Why this is safe and deterministic.** It keeps AD f15852f8's invariant: the join is read-only over the store, and a store write in the join is a compile error. Every worker's delta holds only facts novel against the same frozen Sₙ, so their union is exactly the Δₙ₊₁ a single worker builds. The frontier, the round count, and every report, capped included, are therefore the same at every W (M1 (e), AD 85f90bba).\n\n**Evidence:**\n- `make determinism` is byte-identical at W ∈ {1,2,4,8} × caps {0, 1, R/2, R−1, R, ∞} over every fixture (978 comparisons, 174 runs actually cut short). `make determinism-corpus` does the same for RO, OBI, GO and EL-GALEN.\n- `make test-tsan` shows no race (86 tests, all on the parallel path).\n- Every golden, corpus hashes included, is unchanged at W = 4.\n- Mutations caught: workers sharing one delta (TSan build crashes), merging only one worker (12 tests fail and the gate fails), freeing worker arenas before the merge (ASan use-after-free).\n\n**Found on the way:**\n- A closure captures a `mut` local BY REFERENCE (`&part` in the C). Spawning a worker on the loop's `mut part` made every thread read a stack slot the next iteration reused, and the litmus failed deterministically. Workers now capture an immutable copy (`share`).\n- The SLOP transpiler resolved `join` to strlib's across the build (fixed upstream in slop PR #173; the same class of bug for types is slop #174)." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/48b331ef-b073-490b-9785-e0afda7485d7> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "superseded" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/48b331ef-b073-490b-9785-e0afda7485d7> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-09-27T17:54:18.988822Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
