<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/4ee4d605-d01c-4259-89cf-e0b417e055ba> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "el++ join combinator: soundness proved, completeness owed to slop" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/4ee4d605-d01c-4259-89cf-e0b417e055ba> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/4ee4d605-d01c-4259-89cf-e0b417e055ba> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Every el++ rule applied over a set of stored partners ((7) on an arriving inst, (15)-(17) on a stored leg, (27)-(29)) goes through ONE combinator, `join` in src/rules/ksc.slop. A `JoinRule` tag (11 values) names the rule and which premise arrived; `join-instance` unpacks the arrived fact and one partner into the rule's premises and calls the per-instance function; `join-conclusion` turns its Concl into an Option; `join` walks a list snapshot of the partners (no maps, breaks or c-inline).\n\n**Proved:** `join`'s soundness, `(forall (c $result) (exists (q ps) (== (join-conclusion tag t q ax) (some c))))`, as a @post through a checked @loop-invariant (slop #228). The invariant must be stated over the Option-returning call: a field projected from a call's record result, `(. (join-instance …) fires)`, is not linked between body and invariant (probed: fails \"not preserved\"). A bare Bool field as the filter test crashes the verifier (Z3 sort mismatch), so the body writes `(== … true)`.\n\n**Owed, not claimed:** completeness, \"every partner's firing head is returned\". slop models a for-each element only as SOME member of the list, never the visited prefix, so the verifier REFUTES even a one-line filter's completeness with an empty result (probed on Int elements too, so it is not about records). A refuted contract cannot stand in the tree, so it is a stated comment, not a @property. `join-instance` and `join-conclusion` carry no contracts: the links would be field projections of call results. Per Constraint 01c06881 the remedy is upstream: a for-each model that knows its visited prefix (or interprets list-get on a tracked sequence for an indexed loop).\n\n**Held meanwhile by:** the engine-vs-reference differential (test-ksc-engine-matches-reference): on 15 el++ fixtures the prototype engine answers every unsat(A) and holds(A,B) as the literal Psc reference does, which shares nothing with the engine but the proved per-instance functions." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
