<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/50f5ac71-5745-4a2c-9144-436b737b5c6e> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#ArchitecturalDecision> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/50f5ac71-5745-4a2c-9144-436b737b5c6e> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "The §12 benchmark times certified inputs and answers from axioms in hand to taxonomy" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/50f5ac71-5745-4a2c-9144-436b737b5c6e> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/50f5ac71-5745-4a2c-9144-436b737b5c6e> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "`make bench` (bench/bench.py, results in bench/results.txt) implements SPEC §12's protocol with the classification window running from axioms in hand to the taxonomy, on both sides.\n\n**Classification window.**\n- **The oracle.** Reasoner creation + consistency check + `precomputeInferences`, over an `OWLOntology` built by its untimed parse. The OWL API parse does both the text and the RDF-to-OWL mapping. ELK 0.6.0 then loads, normalizes and indexes the axioms lazily at the first query, and HermiT does so in its constructor. Both are inside the window.\n- **HOWL.** `prepare_ms + reason_ms`: gate, normalize, rename, initialize, premise index, saturation and extraction, over the axioms built by its untimed parse and decode.\n- **Decode.** The front end is split at `decode-document` / `normalize-decoded` (howl.slop `decode` + `prepare-decoded`, with `prepare` as their composition, so the library path is unchanged). The CLI's `--timings` line is `parse_ms decode_ms prepare_ms reason_ms total_ms`. bench.py records `howl_decode_ms` beside each entry. `bench.py check` refuses a results file written under the old boundary (no `howl_decode_ms`).\n\n**Unchanged from the superseded decision.**\n- **W = 4 on both sides.**\n- **Median of 5 runs after 1 warm-up.**\n- **Routing.** ELK gates GO and EL-GALEN; HermiT reports RO and OBI.\n- **Certified input and answer on every run.** The content check, the `howl-report` and `oracle-entailments` pins, and `fixpoint` / `omitted 0`.\n- **Verdict from the recorded medians.**\n- **Load recorded.**\n\n**Evidence.**\n- Every report is unchanged across the full gate suite.\n- Codex review found no library-path change. Its two findings were fixed: `check` accepted old-boundary results, and the `total_ms` comment claimed report printing was timed." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
