<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/5570d76e-8682-4300-965e-025884269d65> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#ArchitecturalDecision> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/5570d76e-8682-4300-965e-025884269d65> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "el++ calculus is Krötzsch's Ksc, with one shared saturation for safe classes" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/5570d76e-8682-4300-965e-025884269d65> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/5570d76e-8682-4300-965e-025884269d65> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "The `el++` rung implements Krötzsch's materialisation calculus Ksc (KIT TR 3005, 2010, Theorem 2), which is sound and complete for classification of SROEL(⊓,×). It is the one published proof that covers nominals together with ⊥, role hierarchies, chains with the OWL 2 EL range restriction, ranges and Self.\n\nHOWL changes Ksc's representation in three ways, each proved in SPEC §5.4:\n\n**K2, sharing by monotonicity.** G, the closure of Kinst, is computed once. A class q that needs its own run starts from `G ∪ {inst(q, q)}` and stores only the facts not already in G.\n\n**K3, rule (4) as a flag.** ⊥ under q may arise at any element. Inconsistency is `unsat(owl:Thing)`, not \"⊥ in G\": with no individuals, ⊤ ⊑ ⊥ leaves G empty.\n\n**K6, one shared saturation for safe classes** (accepted 2026-10-01).\n- **W** is the closure of every queried class's seed `inst(A, A)` plus the individuals, under Fig. 3 without rule (4). This is [Krö10] Theorem 3's construction.\n- **Safe:** an element is safe when no element its triples reach is an individual or holds a nominal in W.\n- **A safe class is answered from W.** Its run equals G plus W's facts about its cone, so it is unsatisfiable iff ⊥ is in G or in its cone.\n- **An unsafe class runs over G ∪ W_S** (W's facts about safe elements). ⊥ is detected through committed triples into safe elements whose cone holds ⊥.\n- **A W cut short by the cap answers nothing.**\n- **Effect:** a nominal-free ontology is one saturation, as in `el` and ELK.\n\n**Translation (K0, K1):**\n- Ranges are native products, `R ⊑ ⊤×D`.\n- Domains are `∃R.⊤ ⊑ C`, not products.\n- `ReflexiveObjectProperty(R)` becomes `⊤ ⊑ ∃S_R.Self` and `S_R ⊑ R`, with `S_R` fresh and simple.\n- `owl:bottomObjectProperty` becomes `∃N.⊤ ⊑ ⊥`.\n- Inclusions into `owl:topObjectProperty` are dropped.\n- Rules (19)–(22) are not implemented: their EDB predicates are always empty.\n\n**Engine:** new, and separate from `el`'s. Phases run in order G, W, then unsafe classes in parallel. `rounds` = `rounds(G)` + `rounds(W)` + the most rounds any single unsafe q took.\n\n**Registration:** `BoundedDl`, because EL++ includes concrete domains.\n\nEvidence: SPEC.md §5.4 (K0–K6). TR 3005 Definition 1, Figs. 1–3, Proposition 1, Theorems 1–3. KKS12 Theorem 4 (ELO only)." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
