<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/6135b9b3-1a57-4eab-9a0a-0ae9994ed5c3> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#weighs> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Alternative/8cde5c22-1c08-4ad7-a802-62c126cdfef7> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/62a5114f-89a3-46ac-b54b-06625b930b0d> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#ArchitecturalDecision> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/62a5114f-89a3-46ac-b54b-06625b930b0d> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "el++ reads role inclusions through the told closure (K7)" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/62a5114f-89a3-46ac-b54b-06625b930b0d> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/62a5114f-89a3-46ac-b54b-06625b930b0d> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "el++ no longer materialises [Krö10] rule (13). A triple is stored once, under the role it was derived with. A premise triple(x, v, y) is read as \"some triple(x, e, y) is stored with e ∈ sub*(v)\", where sub* is the told role hierarchy's reflexive-transitive closure. This is el's L6 (M1 6b) carried to Ksc. Rule (14) stays materialised. Rules (2) and (29) apply at the stored role.\n\n**The claim** (SPEC §5.4 K7): the stored facts, read through sub*, are exactly Psc's closure with (13). It is proved both ways, as closure arguments.\n\n**Consequences for the rest of §5.4:**\n- K2–K6 are stated over Psc's closure, so they hold as written.\n- K6's cones depend only on triple endpoints, which K7 does not change.\n- Reports are equal on complete runs only. Under a cap, K7 can reach a consequence rounds earlier.\n\n**Why:** on EL-GALEN, rule (13)'s super-role copies are most of W's 8.4M triples, which is behind the 10.3 GB peak (Consequence efaaa568).\n\n**Accepted 2026-10-02 (PR #16), under the owner's condition: K7 must not break el++ conformance.** Before it ships, three checks must all come back identical:\n1. **Against the published rules.** The literal reference evaluator keeps rule (13). The engine must agree with it on new targeted fixtures: chain legs under sub-roles in both arrival orders, Self on a sub-role, (29) re-pointing, ranges on super-roles, role cycles, and K6's boundary through a sub-role.\n2. **Against an independent oracle.** Every W3C/ELK conformance ontology inside el++ must give its stated result, with HermiT used where the suite states none.\n3. **Against the engine before K7.** Per-class answers must be identical on every fixture, OBI, GO and EL-GALEN.\n\nA single difference withholds K7.\n\n**Codex review:** no counterexample. Its three textual findings are fixed: complete runs only for the report-equality claim; §5.4's introduction and §7 now name K6 and K7; and the gate's independent oracles." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
