<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/6327c225-293b-4ed0-a9ba-5ebb70551104> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "The ABox encoding is justified by a nominal-free reduction and a canonical model" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/6327c225-293b-4ed0-a9ba-5ebb70551104> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/6327c225-293b-4ed0-a9ba-5ebb70551104> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "SPEC §5.3 discharges M1 (f), the soundness and completeness argument for the direct-edge ABox encoding. The project owner accepted it on 2026-09-30, and re-accepted the revised route (L1, L5, L8) the same day, after two further adversarial Codex passes.\n\n**Sources:**\n- [BBL05] IJCAI 2005, Lemma 3 (CR1–CR11). Used for SOUNDNESS on any CBox. Its completeness is used only on nominal-free input, because [KKS12] (KR 2012, Example 5) shows it fails with nominals.\n- [BBL08] OWLED 2008. §3 gives the chain/range restriction that the gate enforces. Lemma 1: range elimination via X_{r,D}.\n\n**The route:** O → T_ν (the ABox as nominal GCIs, {a} replaced by I_a) → T_n (normal form) → T_e (ranges eliminated) → T_H (X_{r,{b}} collapsed onto I_b). HOWL then runs the calculus on T_H′: T_H without its nominal axioms, with I_a read as plain class names.\n\n**Lemmas:**\n- L1: the ABox as nominals.\n- L2: normal form, as a conservative extension. This covers key injectivity, left-associated chains, and the ⊥ forms.\n- L3: range elimination, in its stronger form.\n- L4: X_{r,{b}} = {b}, so the direct edge plus the range seeds is exact.\n- L5: I_a ∈ S(C) only if C = I_a.\n- L6: the told-closure role hierarchy equals CR10/CR11.\n- L7: every addressed context is seeded.\n- L8: soundness via Lemma 3's if-direction on T_H′ ⊆ T_H. Completeness via the canonical model of T_H′, checked axiom form by axiom form; each I_a in it is a singleton (by L5), so it is a model of T_H. This gives detect-inconsistent (⊥ ∈ S(⊤) or some ⊥ ∈ S(I_a)) and entails-sub.\n- L9: soundness under partial coverage." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
