<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/746ee2d5-16e2-44f2-b952-c33769e66041> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#ArchitecturalDecision> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/746ee2d5-16e2-44f2-b952-c33769e66041> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "el++ commits in parallel over a store sharded by element" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/746ee2d5-16e2-44f2-b952-c33769e66041> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/746ee2d5-16e2-44f2-b952-c33769e66041> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "At W > 1, phases G and W commit each round on up to W threads (src/kscsat.slop `commit-parallel`), and the result is identical to the serial commit's. This refines AD 1db0fb50's serial commit and takes up its deferred Alternative 5abe3365.\n\n**The store is sharded.** `KStore` holds a list of `Shard`s, one per committer arena. Each shard holds the eight collections (`seen`, insts, noms, holders, outs, ins, noms-at, bots). Every collection is keyed by an element id, and `shard-at` picks the shard as `key mod S`:\n- the subject keys `seen`, insts, noms, outs, noms-at and bots;\n- a triple's other end keys ins;\n- the nominal's element keys holders.\n\nPhase Q's runs and W = 1 use one shard and the serial commit (`commit-serial`).\n\n**The commit has three steps:**\n1. **Subject pass**, parallel. Committer k walks every conclusion in Δₙ's order, taking those whose subject's shard it owns (`shard mod nc == k`). It dedups each against that shard's `seen`, files the subject's half (`file-subject`), and keeps the new ones with their positions.\n2. **Merge**, serial. It walks the conclusions again and rebuilds Δₙ₊₁ in Δₙ's order. It counts the new facts, raises K3's flag, and lists each new fact's other end.\n3. **Other pass**, parallel. Committer k files the other end's half (`file-other`) for each listed fact whose other end's shard it owns.\n\n**Why it equals the serial commit:**\n- A fact is deduplicated in one shard, in Δₙ's order, so the first occurrence wins.\n- Every key's list, and every key's role map, gets the same puts in the same order.\n- The merge restores Δₙ's order.\n\n**Stop-at-bottom.** A round that could raise the flag in a run that stops at ⊥ commits serially (`parallel-commit-ok`, `any-bottom-coded`), because only the serial commit stops at the first ⊥. That happens in at most one round per run.\n\n**Arenas.** Committer k writes only in cas[k] and names it on every put (`:arena`, slop #278), because a shard can change owner between rounds. `classify-renamed` makes the arenas and frees them once the answers have been copied out." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/746ee2d5-16e2-44f2-b952-c33769e66041> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
