<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/746ee2d5-16e2-44f2-b952-c33769e66041> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#resultsIn> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/2e49fa80-754d-4f4a-9632-e7686544ef91> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/7910309f-70ea-4f71-a3bf-8e4d753c05b2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#ArchitecturalDecision> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/7910309f-70ea-4f71-a3bf-8e4d753c05b2> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "el++'s store keeps facts as dense ids, decoded at the rule boundary" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/7910309f-70ea-4f71-a3bf-8e4d753c05b2> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/7910309f-70ea-4f71-a3bf-8e4d753c05b2> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "The el++ engine's store (src/kscsat.slop, src/kscids.slop) keeps each fact as a 16-byte CFact {kind U8, a U32, b U32, c U32}. Each index entry is the single U32 its key doesn't already give: the term of an inst, or the other end of a triple.\n\n**Unchanged.** The rules, the deltas and ksc-join still see KFact. `commit` and `store-holds` encode; the partner readers decode.\n\n**Ids are arithmetic** over the Ints kscnames already renamed classes, roles and witnesses to:\n\n| Kind | Arithmetic id | Table id |\n|---|---|---|\n| element | e-aux w → 3w; class k-fresh n → 3n+1 | 3i+2 |\n| term | k-fresh n → 2n | 2i+1 |\n| role | fresh-role n → 2n | 2i+1 |\n\n- **The table** holds only IRI-carrying values: individuals, nominals, owl:Thing and owl:Nothing (fixed slots matched by string), and named roles.\n- **It is built before any run**, because phase Q reads it from several threads.\n- **Totality** comes from enumerating the constructors rule heads use. A value outside it, or an Int past its scheme's U32 bound, aborts loudly instead of losing a fact.\n\n**Why no lemma.** The encoding is a bijection on what it covers, like the dense renaming (AD 072fdfe9 for el; kscnames for el++).\n\n**Tests.**\n- test-ksc-ids-round-trip: every Psc fact round-trips on every fixture, both on input names and on renamed ones.\n- test-ksc-g-matches-reference: the stored G equals Psc's G fact for fact, through K7.\n- Fixture 31 forces rule (28) through holders. Ksc's nominal rules are otherwise redundant enough that no answer-level test observes that path.\n\n**Mutants.** All four are caught: class/aux tag collision, term decode tag, owl:Thing's fixed element id, and holders keyed by subject." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
