<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/85f90bba-3140-46ac-aa9f-47d76dbd2064> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#weighs> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Alternative/9d9199bb-a022-4419-8b28-8f39a218488a> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/88e84975-f11a-4e4a-b4ff-6b36eb5b5179> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#ArchitecturalDecision> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/88e84975-f11a-4e4a-b4ff-6b36eb5b5179> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "The ABox encoding is justified by reduction to EL++ nominals and range elimination" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/88e84975-f11a-4e4a-b4ff-6b36eb5b5179> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/88e84975-f11a-4e4a-b4ff-6b36eb5b5179> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "M1 (f) is discharged by SPEC §5.3, a written soundness and completeness argument for the direct-edge ABox encoding. The project owner accepted it on 2026-09-30, after four adversarial Codex passes. The argument is a reduction to published results, plus the steps where HOWL's encoding differs from them, which are proved in the spec.\n\n**Published results:**\n- [BBL05] Baader, Brandt, Lutz, \"Pushing the EL Envelope\", IJCAI 2005. Lemma 3: CR1–CR11, including the nominal rule CR6, are sound and complete for normalized EL++ CBoxes with nominals.\n- [BBL08] \"Pushing the EL Envelope Further\", OWLED 2008. §3 gives the chain/range restriction that HOWL's gate enforces. Lemma 1: range elimination via X_{r,D} preserves concept-name subsumption.\n\n**The route:** O → T_ν (the ABox as nominal GCIs, {a} replaced by I_a) → T_n (normal form) → T_e (ranges eliminated) → T_H (X_{r,{b}} collapsed onto I_b) → HOWL's saturation → the report.\n\n**Lemmas proved in the spec:**\n- L1: ABox as nominals.\n- L2: the normal form is a conservative extension. This covers key injectivity, left-associated chains preserving the restriction, and ⊥ forms treated as sinks.\n- L3: range elimination in the stronger form its proof gives (same concept and nominal extensions).\n- L4: X_{r,{b}} = {b}, so the direct edge plus range seeds is exact, including the empty-range case.\n- L5: CR6 never fires, and dropping the {a} contexts is harmless because no edge enters them.\n- L6: the lazy told-closure role hierarchy equals CR10 and CR11.\n- L7: no rule addresses an unregistered context on complete input.\n- L8: Lemma 3 maps onto detect-inconsistent and entails-sub.\n- L9: soundness under partial coverage.\n\n**Correction to the earlier explanation:** identity is lost through range elimination's per-role X_{r,{b}}, not through ∃ itself." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/88e84975-f11a-4e4a-b4ff-6b36eb5b5179> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "superseded" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/88e84975-f11a-4e4a-b4ff-6b36eb5b5179> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-09-30T17:51:39.393856Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
