<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/892b3836-2431-48e4-9b00-60993c930068> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "el++ rules return a firing flag and a fixed head" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/892b3836-2431-48e4-9b00-60993c930068> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/892b3836-2431-48e4-9b00-60993c930068> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Each [Krö10] Fig. 3 rule instance in src/rules/ksc.slop is a @pure, loop-free function over exactly the rule's premises. The premises are written as their fields, in the rule's order, EDB axiom first. It returns `Concl {fires Bool, fact KFact}`:\n- `fact` is the rule's head over these premises, built unconditionally;\n- `fires` says whether the body matches, computed with nested `if`s.\n\n**Contracts.** They read as the three parts of the Datalog rule:\n- `sound`: fires only if the body matches;\n- `complete`: fires whenever it does;\n- `head`: fact is the head over the premises' own terms, which is the K2 provenance condition.\n\nRules (1), (3) and the seed (*) always fire, so they carry `complete` and `head` only. Nested terms in a head are built through constructor helpers in types.slop (`name-term`, `ind-elem`, ...). The contracts call those helpers too, so a head is written the same way in body and contract.\n\n**Examples.** Each rule has one firing and one non-firing case as `@example :eq concl-eq` beside its contracts: 50, plus 2 on the ⊥ flag. They need slop #252.\n\n**Mutants.** All 112 are seen to fail to verify, and every rule mutant is refuted by exactly its contract. The mutations:\n- force fires true or false;\n- drop each join condition;\n- swap a head term." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/892b3836-2431-48e4-9b00-60993c930068> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
