<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/8c12dc86-3434-47e9-ab7d-3dd12d828cbe> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "The input is encoded once at the boundary; slop-rdf types stay at the interfaces" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/8c12dc86-3434-47e9-ab7d-3dd12d828cbe> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/8c12dc86-3434-47e9-ab7d-3dd12d828cbe> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "HOWL encodes its input once, at the boundary, into its own internal form, and keeps slop-rdf's types only at the interfaces.\n- **Interfaces:** the port's `List Triple` in, the CLI's streamed parse, and the `IRI`s in the Outcome and report.\n- **Internal form (`termstore.slop`, `Encoded`):** a dictionary holding one owned copy of each distinct term, plus the triples as id triples in document order, duplicates kept.\n- **The user's direction:** slop-rdf types matter for interoperability, but the internal representation should be whatever is best. This complements AD 17beb51b: HOWL and GROWL compose through RDF.\n\n**Mechanics:**\n- **`intern-owned`** copies a term's strings on first sight: the IRI, and a literal's value, datatype and lang. It rebuilds a quoted triple from its parts' owned terms, keyed structurally. Blank ids are kept, since reports print them.\n- **`encoded-add`** shifts a document's blank ids in subject and object, recursing into quoted triples, by `encoded-next-document`'s offset: the highest blank id encoded so far, plus 1. That is exactly the CLI's old list merge.\n- **Stage 0 and decode run on ids.** Sets of ids replace term comparisons, since equal terms share one id. A `Triple` is materialized from the dictionary only where decode reads terms.\n- **Indexes are over a shared dictionary** (`store-over` / `store-insert-ids`). Decode's store indexes only the 21 predicates its queries ask about (`decode-store`), and `test-decode-store-answers-as-the-full-store` holds it to a full store's answers.\n- **The CLI** streams each document through slop-rdf's existing `parse-ttl-file-for-each-triple` into the encoder, in a parse arena freed as soon as that parse returns. No `List Triple` is built. `parse_ms` now includes encoding.\n\n**Evidence:**\n- **Reports:** every report is byte-identical, including a new `-I` golden (F0).\n- **Codex review:** no defects.\n- **Mutations:**\n  - a parser string left un-owned → `golden-asan` red (82 runs);\n  - the import offset off by one → the `-I` golden red;\n  - `owl:members` dropped from `decode-store` → the differential and nine others red;\n  - dropped duplicates are report-invisible, because the gate collapses them." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
