<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/9c8cfc19-668d-4531-a19b-de04280dc826> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#ArchitecturalDecision> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/9c8cfc19-668d-4531-a19b-de04280dc826> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "el++ join combinator: soundness and completeness both proved" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/9c8cfc19-668d-4531-a19b-de04280dc826> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/9c8cfc19-668d-4531-a19b-de04280dc826> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Every el++ rule applied over a set of stored partners goes through ONE combinator, `join`, in src/rules/ksc.slop. That covers (7) on an arriving inst, (15)-(17) on a stored leg, and (27)-(29). A `JoinRule` tag names the rule and which premise arrived. `join-instance` unpacks the arrived fact and one partner into the rule's premises and calls the per-instance function. `join-conclusion` is its Option view. `join` walks a list snapshot of the partners.\n\n**Proved** (slop main 7380645), each a @post through a checked @loop-invariant:\n- **Soundness:** `(forall (c $result) (exists (q ps) (== (join-conclusion tag t q ax) (some c))))`.\n- **Completeness:** `(forall (q ps) (match (join-conclusion tag t q ax) ((some c) (list-contains $result c)) ((none) true)))`. Its invariant quantifies over `(list-visited ps)` (slop #247).\n- **The link between the two:** `join-conclusion` has a proved @post tying its Option to `join-instance`'s Concl fields (slop #251).\n\n**Why an Option view.** Both an Option form and a direct Concl-field form prove on the real code. Over the Option, though, the solver REFUTES broken joins: dropping, skipping or inventing conclusions all report \"loop invariant not preserved\". Over the fields it only times out. A contract should be seen to fail, so the Option form was kept.\n\n**Mutants:**\n- join: drop all, skip the first, and push the trigger. All three are refuted; push-trigger needs make verify's longer solver timeout (60 s).\n- join-conclusion: swapping some and none comes back unknown even at 120 s. It is never verified; the solver cannot build a counter-model through join-instance's body.\n\n`join-instance` has no contract. It is a tag dispatch with one call per arm, and the engine-vs-reference differential covers the argument order it passes." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
