<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/a49e3090-ffd6-4031-9cef-142f290e3b85> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#weighs> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Alternative/f88826e8-d568-48fc-a30c-a64419230b20> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/b09700d9-5b2c-4db9-af2e-8c713cfd04ab> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#ArchitecturalDecision> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/b09700d9-5b2c-4db9-af2e-8c713cfd04ab> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Negation in positive positions is rewritten before the gate" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/b09700d9-5b2c-4db9-af2e-8c713cfd04ab> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/b09700d9-5b2c-4db9-af2e-8c713cfd04ab> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "¬E as the whole filler, or a top-level conjunct, of a superclass, domain or range is rewritten into ⊥ GCIs by a gate pass, `expand-negation` (src/gate.slop). The pass runs after sugar expansion and before every gate condition:\n- C ⊑ P ⊓ ¬E ⇒ C ⊑ P, C ⊓ E ⊑ ⊥\n- dom(r) ⊑ P ⊓ ¬E ⇒ dom(r) ⊑ P, ∃r.⊤ ⊓ E ⊑ ⊥\n- ran(r) ⊑ P ⊓ ¬E ⇒ ran(r) ⊑ P, ∃r.E ⊑ ⊥\n\nNo fresh names are introduced, so the models are the same (SPEC §5.3 L0). The logic stays ELH⊥R+, so no calculus, NormAxiom or report change is needed.\n\n**Why before the gate.** Regularity, the range/composition condition and the declaration check all read the expanded list. Judging the rewritten theory is what lets a negative range impose nothing on a chain's last role: it is the GCI ∃t.E ⊑ ⊥, which range elimination never touches.\n\n**Whole axioms or nothing.** The rewrite applies only when C, every E, every conjunct of P, and the role are in profile. Anything else passes through and is omitted as written. So the only change to existing reports is axioms becoming accepted.\n\n**Why now.** BFO, CCO and RO use domain/range BFO_0000004 ⊓ ¬BFO_0000006 on 9, 11 and 2 axioms respectively. OBI has 2 axioms of the form CL_0000001 ⊑ ¬∃r.E.\n\n**Evidence:**\n- 100/100 unit tests pass, and 4 mutations were each seen red: the ⊥ piece dropped; the range given the domain form; ranges read before the rewrite; a partly-out axiom split.\n- HermiT agrees on 6 new fixtures and probes. HermiT and ELK both pass 3 new probes.\n- The ELK conformance tests Negation, InconsistentNegation, NegationExistential and PropertyRangesNegation moved from outside-v0 to ok.\n- abox-fuzz --negation: 400/400 clean against HermiT (276 inconsistent).\n- The RO and OBI projections are diff-clean against HermiT.\n- Codex adversarial review: no counterexample." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
