<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/b25fcbb1-05d6-4f04-bab4-9515b39f67e7> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#weighs> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Alternative/be8d1173-51d6-402d-9b30-0455079e7a15> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/b33105d0-1542-4db5-9171-bb11179187f1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#ArchitecturalDecision> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/b33105d0-1542-4db5-9171-bb11179187f1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "The round runs on W workers at both the join and the barrier: partitioned commit, no merge" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/b33105d0-1542-4db5-9171-bb11179187f1> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/b33105d0-1542-4db5-9171-bb11179187f1> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "At `worker-count` W > 1 a round runs in five steps (src/saturate.slop):\n1. **Split.** The frontier `active` is divided into up to W contiguous shares.\n2. **Join.** One thread per share runs `round-join-part`. It writes only its own arena and RoundDelta; the store and the premise index are frozen and only read.\n3. **Partition** (serial; `partition-round`, `partition-one`). Walk every delta's keys and give each touched context one owner, round-robin in first-seen order. Also create any context a delta names, which is the round's one registry write (an undeclared class used as a CR3 filler).\n4. **Commit** (parallel; `commit-round`, `commit-bucket`, `commit-entry`). One committer per owner. Each commits its bucket's entries, drawn from every delta, into the contexts it owns, growing their sets in its own long-lived commit arena (`commit-arenas`). A fact is queued only if it was new to the store, which is how two workers' copies of one fact become one.\n5. **Collect** (serial, per touched context). Build the next queues, the frontier and the count.\n\nAt W = 1 the one committer uses the run arena and nothing is spawned: the sequential reference path.\n\n**Why it replaces merge-then-commit (M1 slice 6b C1).** The old barrier was two serial passes over every conclusion: `merge-delta` folded all worker deltas into one, then `round-commit` folded that into the store. On EL-GALEN at W = 4 they were 38% and 30% of the round, so reasoning scaled only 1.4× from W = 1 to W = 4. With the barrier partitioned it scales 2.5× (3.6× at W = 8).\n\n**Result** (bench/results.txt):\n\n| Entry | Before (C0) | After |\n|---|---|---|\n| EL-GALEN | 11.36× ELK | 7.74× |\n| GO | 6.33× ELK | 5.89× |\n\nEvery report is unchanged: goldens, the corpus report hashes, and determinism identical across 2,016 comparisons, capped runs included.\n\n**Why every W gives the same round.** Each fact belongs to one context, and each context has one committer. So the store after the barrier is the union of the deltas, each queue holds each novel fact once, and the frontier is the touched set. Only queue order can differ, and Δ is a set.\n\n**Evidence:**\n- `test-commit-dedups-across-deltas` checks queue contents and both edge halves by content.\n- `undeclared-filler.ttl` drives a mid-run context creation at W = 4 under TSan.\n- Mutations, each seen red:\n  - queueing non-new facts (the dedup test);\n  - a second sighting given a new owner (a TSan race);\n  - creating contexts in the committers (a TSan race);\n  - the pred half queued as a succ (the dedup test and five others).\n- Codex review: no functional defect. Its two points were fixed: the test now checks by content, and the SPEC calls TSan evidence rather than proof.\n\n**Kept:** the rejected alternatives of the superseded record still hold (c-inline pthreads; a channel-arrival merge; ELK-style racing saturation). A newly rejected one: keeping the merge and parallelizing only the commit, which leaves one serial pass over every conclusion." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/b33105d0-1542-4db5-9171-bb11179187f1> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
