<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/b36adc54-6a36-49c7-bb41-a4744cb6caab> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Context owns the derived facts; Saturation owns the round's queues" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/b36adc54-6a36-49c7-bb41-a4744cb6caab> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#isMotivatedBy> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/65db656d-afe2-49bc-80aa-0d3677bca2e9> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/b36adc54-6a36-49c7-bb41-a4744cb6caab> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#supersedes> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/ff60d323-bdc6-4e9a-ae99-acb6e214e62f> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/bb7b652d-6f69-45d2-9c3d-507b9e389157> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#ArchitecturalDecision> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/bb7b652d-6f69-45d2-9c3d-507b9e389157> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "ABox encoding: class assertions to GCIs, role assertions to edges" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/bb7b652d-6f69-45d2-9c3d-507b9e389157> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/bb7b652d-6f69-45d2-9c3d-507b9e389157> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Class and role assertions are encoded ASYMMETRICALLY, and the asymmetry is essential rather than incidental.\n- `C(a)` becomes the pre-normalization GCI `individual(a) ⊑ C`.\n- `r(a,b)` becomes an EDGE emitted into Δ₀ via `emit-edge(individual(a), r, individual(b))`, plus `derived-sub(A)` to `individual(b)` for every A in ran_T(r). It is NOT the GCI `individual(a) ⊑ ∃r.individual(b)`.\n\n**Why role assertions are not existentials.** As semantics the existential reading is weaker (\"some member of individual(b)\"), but the calculus alone would keep the identity: CR3 sends ∃r.individual(b) to the one individual(b) context. What loses it is RANGE ELIMINATION, which rewrites C ⊑ ∃r.D into C ⊑ ∃r.X_{r,D}, with one fresh X per role. So r(a,b) and s(c,b) would reach two contexts, X_{r,b} and X_{s,b}, each carrying only its own role's range. The counterexample: DisjointClasses(C,D), range(r)=C, range(s)=D, r(a,b), s(c,b) is inconsistent, yet under the existential encoding HOWL would report COHERENT. The direct edge with its seeds is the eliminated form collapsed back onto individual(b), and SPEC §5.3 (L4) proves that collapse exact, because individual(b) stands for one element. An earlier draft justified the existential form by noting that nothing in a nominal-free fragment can force two DISTINCT individuals to be equal. That is true and irrelevant: the failure is one name occurring twice.\n\n**Two consequences of the edge form that are not optional.**\n- Edges enter through Δ₀, never by a direct write to succs/preds. The rules fire on edge deltas: CR4 and CR5 on each half, and CR7 (chains), with role inclusions matched through the told closure. A stored-only edge would leave hierarchies and chains applying to derived edges but not asserted ones.\n- Ranges are seeded at installation, because the published range-elimination rewrite touches existential GCIs only.\n\n**Punning.** Each individual is a concept name in a SEPARATE TAGGED NAMESPACE. OWL permits class/individual punning, so without the tag a class `:x ⊑ ⊥` and an unrelated individual `:x` would merge into one context and manufacture a FALSE inconsistency.\n\n**Status.** Proved sound and complete in SPEC §5.3 (M1 (f), accepted 2026-09-30; AD 88e84975).\n\n**Why it is in v0 at all.** It unblocks the first consumer: under the stub HOWL replaces, every instance-bearing delta is inconclusive.\n\nEvidence: SPEC.md §5.2, §5.3, §6.2, §10 test 13 (the mandatory regression fixture), §13." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/bb7b652d-6f69-45d2-9c3d-507b9e389157> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
