<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/fa55e24c-719a-417d-b4c5-3a84f15367ab> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#ArchitecturalDecision> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/fa55e24c-719a-417d-b4c5-3a84f15367ab> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Dispatch does each join once, from its cheaper side" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/fa55e24c-719a-417d-b4c5-3a84f15367ab> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/fa55e24c-719a-417d-b4c5-3a84f15367ab> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "M1 slice 6b step A removed redundant work from saturation, without changing a single report: goldens were byte-identical, round counts included, and the RO/OBI/GO/EL-GALEN report hashes were unchanged.\n\n1. **`admit` handles a logical edge once, through its successor half.** `derived-pred` is a documented no-op. Every predecessor half on the admit path arrives with its successor sibling in the same rule output, because `emit-edge` is its only constructor and seeds bypass `admit`.\n2. **CR2, and CR4's on-edge trigger, walk the smaller side of their join.** This is ELK's lazy set intersection. premise.slop's two-level `Partners` buckets make it possible: `and-by-pair` maps a conjunct to its partner conjuncts, and `lhs-by-role` maps a role to its fillers, each with a count of inner keys. The dispatcher compares that count with |S(X)|, walks the smaller side and probes the other. Each surviving axiom still goes through the unchanged, proved rule function. Since D2, CR4's on-edge walk runs once per role in sup*(e).\n\n(Step A also made CR6 fire from the successor half only, deleting `cr-role-incl-on-pred`: 3.2M redundant messages on EL-GALEN. D2 then deleted CR6 itself; see AD 017b993e.)\n\n**Measured call counts at step A (single-threaded):**\n\n| Measure | EL-GALEN | GO |\n|---|---|---|\n| CR2 calls | 14.9M → 488k | 77.2M → 131k |\n| CR4 on-edge calls | 27.8M → 579k | 1.48M → 428k |\n| Edge admits | 7.71M → 2.24M | 0.97M → 0.44M |\n\n**Verification at step A:**\n- Every gate passed.\n- Mutations: CR2's S(X)-walk with the wrong key, CR2's partner-walk inverted, and CR4's S(Y)-walk with the wrong key were each seen red.\n- hazards/smaller-side-join.ttl was added because no fixture entered the context-side branch.\n- Codex review: one comment correction." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
