<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/2a0638d0-8948-4ff9-8d51-18788fa4cb52> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Parallel rounds roughly halve reasoning time at 4 workers; prepare now dominates GO" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/2a0638d0-8948-4ff9-8d51-18788fa4cb52> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/2a0638d0-8948-4ff9-8d51-18788fa4cb52> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Measured single-run with --timings on this machine (arm64, 28 cores, 96 GB), W = 1 against W = 4 (two runs each). This is not the S6 benchmark protocol:\n- **GO:** reason_ms 5,952 / 5,689 → 2,942 / 3,523, about 1.8×.\n- **EL-GALEN:** reason_ms 20,731 / 18,181 → 8,067 / 9,569, about 2.2×.\n\nGO's `prepare` (normalize and the premise index, 7–8.6 s) is single-threaded and now exceeds its reasoning time. It is the next thing S6's profile should look at. The ordered merge and the per-worker arenas cost less than the speedup buys, so no work stealing or dynamic balancing is attempted in S5." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
