<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/3f867247-4d7b-46c2-bbfd-0c89eadced9e> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#resultsFrom> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/b1b29794-7999-4d7d-9ec3-9ab0c63967e7> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/422e9153-dc25-4298-908f-94f77a29f9e7> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Consequence> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/422e9153-dc25-4298-908f-94f77a29f9e7> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "The ABox proof obligation is discharged (SPEC §5.3); assertions are inside the sound-and-complete claim" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/422e9153-dc25-4298-908f-94f77a29f9e7> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/422e9153-dc25-4298-908f-94f77a29f9e7> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "The direct-edge ABox encoding, which is HOWL's own construction, is proved sound and complete in SPEC §5.3 by reduction to [BBL05] (EL++ with nominals, Lemma 3) and [BBL08] (range elimination, Lemma 1), plus nine lemmas for the steps specific to HOWL. Its theorem: with empty coverage.omitted and fixpoint termination, `inconsistent`, `unsat` and `entails-sub` over the input signature are exactly O's entailments; under partial coverage or a cap, every reported finding is entailed. So assertions now ship INSIDE the v0 sound-and-complete claim. README's † on ClassAssertion and ObjectPropertyAssertion now points at §5.3. make abox-fuzz and the ABox fixtures check the code against the argument." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/422e9153-dc25-4298-908f-94f77a29f9e7> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
