<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/48af4a2f-3e41-432c-9eb2-9f399a2b7afa> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Consequence> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/48af4a2f-3e41-432c-9eb2-9f399a2b7afa> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "HOWL adopts slop #278: el's parallel commit names :arena, el++'s arena helpers removed" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/48af4a2f-3e41-432c-9eb2-9f399a2b7afa> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/48af4a2f-3e41-432c-9eb2-9f399a2b7afa> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "2026-10-03. HOWL's csrc was regenerated with slop main df93c3a (#278, collections grow in their own arena).\n\n**Changes:**\n- **`src/saturate.slop`:** `:arena arena` added to the store puts in `commit-sub`, `commit-succ` and `commit-pred`, and to `commit-entry`'s `qs.by-node` put. Committers grow collections other threads made, so each names its own arena. Remove the `qs.by-node` one and TSan reports a race in `slop_map_put` from `commit-entry`.\n- **`src/kscsat.slop`:** the el++ helpers `delta-push`, `cfact-push` and `put-chunk` are removed and their stale comments rewritten. Each collection is made in the arena it should grow in.\n\n**Checks:**\n- `make test`, `test-asan` and `test-tsan` pass: 116 each, zero sanitizer reports.\n- Every golden is unchanged: el, el++, and the el++ `rounds` lines.\n- `crate-test` passes. No FFI-mirrored struct holds a list or map, so the List header's new `arena` field changed no guarded layout.\n\n**Records:** Lesson 6245f8b5 is superseded by c75e8926, and Lesson 7cd9a031 is retracted." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/48af4a2f-3e41-432c-9eb2-9f399a2b7afa> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/48af4a2f-3e41-432c-9eb2-9f399a2b7afa> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-10-03T16:57:41.840869Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/48af4a2f-3e41-432c-9eb2-9f399a2b7afa> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "HOWL adopts slop #278: el's parallel commit names :arena, el++'s arena helpers removed" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/4b289892-b531-4510-a6f1-c7e333e97c34> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Consequence> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/4b289892-b531-4510-a6f1-c7e333e97c34> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "K7 cuts EL-GALEN to 4.2 s and 3.2 GB; the gate found no difference" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/4b289892-b531-4510-a6f1-c7e333e97c34> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/4b289892-b531-4510-a6f1-c7e333e97c34> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "This is the measured effect of K7 (el++ reads role inclusions through the told closure) in slice 6's engine, 2026-10-02.\n\n**Measurements.** Reasoning time is single-threaded G and W; peak is `howl validate --profile el++ --workers 1`.\n\n| | Before K7 (K6 only) | With K7 |\n|---|---|---|\n| EL-GALEN W facts | 10.3M | 3.3M |\n| EL-GALEN rounds | 32 | 27 |\n| EL-GALEN time | 8.7 s | 4.2 s |\n| EL-GALEN peak | 11.6 GB | 3.24 GB (`el`: 0.46 GB) |\n| GO time | 1.2 s | 1.0 s |\n| GO peak | — | 1.30 GB (`el`: 0.59 GB) |\n| OBI time | — | 0.15 s |\n\n- **The first K7 build was slower.** It walked `sub*(v)` per stored leg and took EL-GALEN to 11.9 s. Walking the smaller side fixed it: either the roles stored at the element, tested with `e ⊑* v`, or `sub*(v)` looked up at the element.\n\n**The gate (owner's condition) found no difference anywhere:**\n- **Reference differential:** agrees on all 29 el++ fixtures, including 8 new K7 fixtures.\n- **Conformance:** the 115 ontologies inside el++ whole all give their stated results (0 FAIL). HermiT agrees with 113; it cannot load the other 2.\n- **Against the engine before K7:** identical apart from `rounds` on all 146 conformance reports, all 98 corpus fixtures, and every class of OBI, GO and EL-GALEN.\n- **Mutation testing:** 8 read-through mutants and 2 cancellation mutants were all caught.\n\n**Memory is still above the target** of ≤ 2 GB and ≤ 2× el. The remaining cost is representation:\n- each fact is stored by value (96 B) in the dedup set and again in 2 indexes;\n- lists grown in the arena keep their old buffers;\n- on EL-GALEN, W's dedup set takes about 0.45 GB and the index lists about 1.3 GB.\n\nThe next step is the plan's step 3, a compact fact encoding." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/4b289892-b531-4510-a6f1-c7e333e97c34> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/4b289892-b531-4510-a6f1-c7e333e97c34> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-10-02T02:56:10.384213Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
