<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/507612c5-1352-4887-b5fb-a5c16525e0ea> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Consequence> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/507612c5-1352-4887-b5fb-a5c16525e0ea> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "A context created mid-run for an undeclared filler gets no seeds, so INCONCLUSIVE runs can under-derive" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/507612c5-1352-4887-b5fb-a5c16525e0ea> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/507612c5-1352-4887-b5fb-a5c16525e0ea> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "When an accepted axiom `A ⊑ ∃r.B` names a class B that was never declared, the gate records B's missing declaration (the verdict is INCONCLUSIVE) and keeps the axiom. B is not in `signature-nodes`, so its context is created only when the edge (A, r, B) first reaches the barrier (`ensure-context`, now in `partition-round`), with an empty store. No seeds are delivered: B ∉ S(B) and ⊤ ∉ S(B).\n\n**Consequence.** Rules that need those facts never fire at B. With `domain(r) = C`, i.e. `∃r.⊤ ⊑ C`, CR4 at B never sees ⊤ ∈ S(B), so the entailed `A ⊑ C` is NOT derived. The run is already INCONCLUSIVE, so no false coherent verdict results. It is sound, but the subsumptions reported are incomplete.\n\n**Pinned, not fixed** (M1 slice 6b C1). `hazards/undeclared-filler.ttl` and its golden show `A ⊑ C` absent, on purpose: the fix (seed a context when it is created mid-run, or include every NormAxiom node in `signature-nodes`) changes reports, and should be its own reviewed change. The golden diff will then show exactly the facts it adds." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/507612c5-1352-4887-b5fb-a5c16525e0ea> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/507612c5-1352-4887-b5fb-a5c16525e0ea> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-09-29T01:06:40.884981Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/507612c5-1352-4887-b5fb-a5c16525e0ea> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "A context created mid-run for an undeclared filler gets no seeds, so INCONCLUSIVE runs can under-derive" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/507612c5-1352-4887-b5fb-a5c16525e0ea> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#resultsFrom> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/5cecf538-1be2-4f57-a979-888812c3b7d4> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/5084ba81-de8a-416a-8a77-615662c6d374> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Consequence> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/5084ba81-de8a-416a-8a77-615662c6d374> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "el++ is differential-tested like el: probes, fixtures, conformance, corpus, fuzz, determinism" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/5084ba81-de8a-416a-8a77-615662c6d374> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/5084ba81-de8a-416a-8a77-615662c6d374> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Slice 6d, 2026-10-02. Every harness takes `--profile el|el++`. el's records are byte-identical except conformance's label rename outside-v0 → outside-el. el++ has its own inputs and records.\n\n| Harness | el++ inputs | Result |\n|---|---|---|\n| Probes | 9 in corpus/fixtures/probes-el++/, each load-bearing for HOWL and HermiT (deleting the construct loses the entailment) | HOWL and HermiT pass all; ELK 3/9 (hasValue, Self on the right, reflexive) |\n| Fixtures | 121 taken whole | all diff-clean against HermiT; ELK gates where both capability records clear it |\n| Conformance | W3C and ELK suites | 105 checkable (81 under el), 0 FAIL |\n| Corpus | el++ projections of RO, OBI, GO, EL-GALEN (corpus/projections/el++/) | RO and OBI clean against HermiT (OBI keeps its hasValue axioms; 38,681 subsumptions); GO and EL-GALEN clean against ELK |\n| `rungs` | the four v0 projections | el and el++ reports identical, profile and rounds aside |\n| abox-fuzz --elpp | 400 generated: nominals, Self on simple roles, reflexive roles, sameAs, differentFrom, AllDifferent, negative assertions | all match HermiT; 211 inconsistent |\n| Determinism | el++ fixtures | every cap 0..R at W ∈ {1,2,4,8}: 5,772 comparisons, 548 capped runs, identical |\n\n**A HermiT fault was found and handled.** HermiT cannot reason over `owl:Thing ⊑ owl:Nothing`: its normalization builds an empty ObjectUnionOf (ExpressionManager.java:454), traced with the oracle's new HOWL_ORACLE_TRACE. differential.py `hermit_faults` marks such fixtures HermiT n/a. ELK must gate them; if it can't, the fixture fails, never passes unchecked.\n\n**Bench is informational**, at W=4:\n\n| | el++ | oracle | ratio | el's ratio |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| OBI | 176 ms | HermiT | 0.05× | — |\n| RO | 17 ms | HermiT | 0.10× | — |\n| GO | 1.26 s | ELK | 2.3× | 0.84× |\n| EL-GALEN | 4.8 s | ELK | 15× | 2.9× |\n\n**Open performance gap.** el++ costs about 1.5–2× el on one thread. The gap widens at W=4 (EL-GALEN 4.8 s against 0.82 s) because el joins each round on worker threads and el++'s phase W, the shared saturation, is single-threaded.\n\n**Codex review**: four findings, all fixed.\n1. Determinism's corpus mode ignored the el++ projections.\n2. A fuzz mode with no recorded line passed.\n3. A HermiT-fault fixture that ELK cannot gate passed unchecked.\n4. The el++ bench header claimed el's ELK gate.\n\nAll 21 gates pass; verify is 80/0/1." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/5084ba81-de8a-416a-8a77-615662c6d374> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/5084ba81-de8a-416a-8a77-615662c6d374> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-10-02T19:23:59.196502Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
