<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/70241867-39be-4d82-942a-9e7f535b9e4e> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "§5.3 re-routed: BBL05 Lemma 3's nominal completeness is refuted (KKS12)" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/70241867-39be-4d82-942a-9e7f535b9e4e> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/70241867-39be-4d82-942a-9e7f535b9e4e> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "SPEC §5.3 (the ABox reduction) applied BBL05 Lemma 3 to a CBox with nominals (`I_a ≡ {a}`). KKS12 (Kazakov, Krötzsch, Simančík, KR 2012) shows that completeness claim false for nominals: \"Although rule (42) is sound, this procedure is not complete for nominals\". Their Example 5, `A ⊑ ∃R.(B ⊓ {o})`, `A ⊑ ∃S.{o}`, `∃S.B ⊑ B`, entails `A ⊑ B`, which the rules miss.\n\n**The theorem is unchanged.** Only the route changed (L1, L5, L8, 2026-09-30):\n- HOWL runs the calculus on the nominal-free `T_H′`, with each `I_a` read as a plain class name.\n- L5 proves `I_a ∈ S(C)` only if `C = I_a`.\n- L8 builds the canonical model of `T_H′`, checking each normal form directly. Each `I_a` is a singleton in it, so it is a model of `T_H`. That gives completeness, and consistency iff `⊥ ∉ S(⊤)` and `⊥ ∉ S(I_a)` for every `a`.\n- Lemma 3 is now used only for soundness, which KKS12 confirms.\n\n**Review.** Codex reviewed the route adversarially over two passes and signed off: no counterexample, and two minor findings fixed. Project-owner re-acceptance is pending. No code changed; `abox-fuzz` (400 seeds against HermiT) stays clean." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
