<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/7fc894a5-4f58-45f7-a04b-c8386aadc5d4> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "slop-rdf's streaming scratch arena cuts the parse phase; OBI and RO peaks fall" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/7fc894a5-4f58-45f7-a04b-c8386aadc5d4> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/7fc894a5-4f58-45f7-a04b-c8386aadc5d4> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "slop-rdf #8 (main e04dd52) bounds streaming Turtle parse memory to one statement, and HOWL's regenerated C is otherwise unchanged. Parse-phase high-water mark: GO 851 -> 474 MB, EL-GALEN 535 -> 63, OBI 236 -> 34, RO 23 -> 5. Overall peaks: OBI 236 -> 142 MB and RO 23 -> 16 (both now in prepare); GO stays 913 (prepare) and EL-GALEN 591 (report), because their peaks were never in the parse. Every report hash unchanged; all 16 gates pass; verify 35/0/1 as before. Only possible because HOWL already streams into an encoded document (the parser's arena is per document and freed at once)." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/7fc894a5-4f58-45f7-a04b-c8386aadc5d4> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/7fc894a5-4f58-45f7-a04b-c8386aadc5d4> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-09-30T06:51:36.084535Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/7fc894a5-4f58-45f7-a04b-c8386aadc5d4> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "slop-rdf's streaming scratch arena cuts the parse phase; OBI and RO peaks fall" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/7fc894a5-4f58-45f7-a04b-c8386aadc5d4> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#resultsFrom> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/8c12dc86-3434-47e9-ab7d-3dd12d828cbe> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/8142f8a0-e32d-4004-99dd-077314c9058a> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Consequence> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/8142f8a0-e32d-4004-99dd-077314c9058a> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Every round's scratch arena leaked until C0: slop's with-arena returned before its free" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/8142f8a0-e32d-4004-99dd-077314c9058a> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/8142f8a0-e32d-4004-99dd-077314c9058a> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "`advance-round` allocated each round's join (rule result lists and delta contexts) in `(with-arena :as scratch …)`, whose value was the commit. slop lowers that to `return saturate_round_commit(...)` placed BEFORE `slop_arena_free(scratch)`, so the free never ran. Every round's scratch stayed resident for the whole run.\n\nThe code's own comment claimed the scratch was \"freed at the barrier\" and that `make test-asan` enforced that nothing escaped it. Neither was true while the free was unreachable.\n\n**The fix (M1 slice 6b C0):** an explicit `arena-new`, then the commit into a let-bound result, then `arena-free`, then return the result.\n- ASan is now actually checking the no-escape claim, and it is clean.\n- Every gate is unchanged.\n\n**Effect** (bench/results.txt, quiet machine):\n- **EL-GALEN:** peak 8.1 → 6.8 GB, 11.36× ELK.\n- **GO:** 6.33× ELK. Its 13.5 GB peak comes from elsewhere, mostly the front end.\n\n**Upstream:** reported for the SLOP agent. A `with-arena` whose body value is the function's return value frees nothing." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/8142f8a0-e32d-4004-99dd-077314c9058a> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/8142f8a0-e32d-4004-99dd-077314c9058a> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-09-29T00:28:53.017738Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/8142f8a0-e32d-4004-99dd-077314c9058a> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Every round's scratch arena leaked until C0: slop's with-arena returned before its free" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/8142f8a0-e32d-4004-99dd-077314c9058a> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#resultsFrom> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/48b331ef-b073-490b-9785-e0afda7485d7> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/81dc85a9-bc11-4320-a371-f72a3092f859> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Consequence> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/81dc85a9-bc11-4320-a371-f72a3092f859> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "The regularity witness still needs a canonical, choice-free policy, because its AxiomRefs are hashed into the consumer's verdict identity." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
