<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/841f255a-ae50-418a-b7d9-b0d3737356b8> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Consequence> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/841f255a-ae50-418a-b7d9-b0d3737356b8> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "S6b profile: HOWL rule redundancy and SLOP runtime hashing split the gap to ELK" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/841f255a-ae50-418a-b7d9-b0d3737356b8> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/841f255a-ae50-418a-b7d9-b0d3737356b8> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "This profiles M1 (c)'s 19x (GO) and 30x (EL-GALEN) gap. The runs were single-threaded, the build was -O2 -g, and I used `sample` call trees plus counters in a scratch copy of the generated C. The causes split into HOWL logic and the SLOP runtime.\n\n**HOWL logic**\n1. **CR6 fires on both halves of every edge.** On EL-GALEN, `role_incl_on_pred` and `role_incl_on_succ` are each called 1.61M times and each emits 3.22M messages, so every super-role edge is derived twice.\n2. **admit tests each half as the full logical edge.** Every new edge is therefore admitted twice. On EL-GALEN there were 7.71M edge admits, of which 5.05M were duplicates within the round and only 1.82M were new; CR6 accounts for 6.4M of them.\n3. **CR2 dispatch walks every conjunction filed under the arriving conjunct.** On GO that is 77.2M calls for 131k conclusions (0.17%), and 23% of reasoning time. ELK iterates the smaller of S(X) and the conjunct's partner set instead (a lazy set intersection).\n4. **CR4's on-edge trigger walks S(Y).** On EL-GALEN that is 27.8M calls for 579k conclusions (2%).\n5. **Every rule call allocates a 16-slot result list,** 1,280 bytes because an Addressed is 80 bytes, even when it returns nothing. Rules return lists instead of taking an accumulator because a (List T) parameter cannot be pushed through in SLOP.\n\n**slop-rdf**\n6. **GO's front end is mostly the triple index build.** `rdf_indexed_graph_add` is 35–40% of the whole GO run. It maintains 4 indexes and does a `contains` check per triple, about 15 full-term hashes, including long literals. HOWL reads only SPO (`objects`, `contains`) and POS (`subjects`); PSO and OSP are built and never read.\n\n**SLOP runtime**\n7. **Generated hash/eq is ~49% of EL-GALEN's reasoning samples and ~33% of GO's.** Counts on EL-GALEN: 135M Node hashes, 263M Node eq calls, 161M `map_get`, 345M probe steps. The underlying costs:\n   - **`slop_map`:** entries store no hash, so every probe calls `eq` through a function pointer (tag, then length, then `memcmp`). Keys are out of line, reached through a pointer. Each probe step does a `%` divide. Growth re-hashes every key and re-copies each key into the arena, leaving the old copies as garbage.\n   - **Strings:** they hash with byte-at-a-time FNV-1a, and `slop_string_eq` has no pointer-equality fast path, although most strings are interned.\n   - **Allocation:** `list-new` eagerly allocates 16 slots, and every Context eagerly creates 3 maps of 16 entries." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/841f255a-ae50-418a-b7d9-b0d3737356b8> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/841f255a-ae50-418a-b7d9-b0d3737356b8> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-09-28T15:37:00.962472Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/841f255a-ae50-418a-b7d9-b0d3737356b8> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "S6b profile: HOWL rule redundancy and SLOP runtime hashing split the gap to ELK" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/841f255a-ae50-418a-b7d9-b0d3737356b8> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#resultsFrom> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/0394c537-72e1-4b00-8079-7d30846b47fa> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/844c16aa-2b1c-4d42-9997-0c9b078b65d2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Consequence> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/844c16aa-2b1c-4d42-9997-0c9b078b65d2> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Barriers idle workers that finish a round early — slower than pure ELK-style racing saturation, accepted as the price of a decision-bearing iteration cap." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
