<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/97b44ce9-6549-42b6-aa0c-6eb414bb7477> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Consequence> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/97b44ce9-6549-42b6-aa0c-6eb414bb7477> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Both round caps are proved: saturate's budget invariant and run-ksc's rounds <= budget (verify 87/0/0)" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/97b44ce9-6549-42b6-aa0c-6eb414bb7477> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/97b44ce9-6549-42b6-aa0c-6eb414bb7477> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "`make verify` is 87 verified, 0 failed, 0 unknown, up from 84/0/1. Both round caps now carry proved contracts:\n- **el:** `saturate`'s budget `@loop-invariant` and `@post` (`iteration <= max-iterations`), with a new `@pre {(. sat iteration) <= (. config max-iterations)}`. That `@pre` only makes explicit what the old `@post` already required.\n- **el++:** `run-ksc`'s `@post {(. $result rounds) <= budget}` (previously owed, held only by test-ksc-cap), through a checked `@loop-invariant` and `@pre {budget >= 0}`.\n\nEach round loop had been shaped in a way slop's loop analysis cannot follow, and all three blockers were bisected with probes:\n1. **A `c-inline` in the loop body.** The cancel-ptr read makes every invariant of its loop unknown. Fixed by moving the read into `types.slop`'s `cancel-requested`, now used at all three sites (filed as slop #280).\n2. **A `record-new` that is the function's result.** Any field read from a `set!` local is left unconstrained (filed as slop #279). It isn't about loops: the same happens with no loop at all. Fixed by building the result in `run-result`, whose `@post` states the field.\n3. **`saturate`'s `break`s, and a call inside the loop handed the Saturation.** Fixed by rewriting the loop with a `going` flag, as `run-ksc` already was, and by changing `budget-exhausted` to take `(iteration max-iterations)` Ints. A minimal probe with a map-carrying record didn't reproduce this one, so it isn't filed.\n\nThe earlier in-source diagnoses were partly wrong. \"A record built after a loop\" was not the trigger: a direct record result is. And \"a call whose arguments carry maps\" was really a call handed the Saturation.\n\n**Behaviour is unchanged.** All 21 gates pass and every golden is unchanged, el++'s rounds lines included. Determinism holds, test-ksc-cap and the cancel tests pass, and ASan and TSan are clean. Codex found no control-flow difference. Its one point, the `@pre`'s comment overclaiming \"every caller\", is fixed." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/97b44ce9-6549-42b6-aa0c-6eb414bb7477> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/97b44ce9-6549-42b6-aa0c-6eb414bb7477> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-10-04T02:40:28.226061Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/97b44ce9-6549-42b6-aa0c-6eb414bb7477> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Both round caps are proved: saturate's budget invariant and run-ksc's rounds <= budget (verify 87/0/0)" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/982f9d9e-c500-48d1-b717-1eabdcaa1d58> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Consequence> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/982f9d9e-c500-48d1-b717-1eabdcaa1d58> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "el++ memory under control: EL-GALEN 0.81 GB (1.8× el), GO 0.62 GB, faster than K7 alone" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/982f9d9e-c500-48d1-b717-1eabdcaa1d58> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/982f9d9e-c500-48d1-b717-1eabdcaa1d58> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Slice 6b part 2 (2026-10-02): the id store, a delta-arena leak fix, and id-level partner counting.\n\n**Reasoning time**, median of 3:\n\n| | before | now |\n|---|---|---|\n| OBI | 0.15 s | 0.15 s |\n| GO | 1.0 s | 0.86 s |\n| EL-GALEN | 4.2 s | 3.75 s |\n\n**Peak memory**, `validate --profile el++ --workers 1`:\n\n| | before | now | el |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| OBI | — | 97 MB | 109 MB |\n| GO | 1.30 GB | 622 MB | 565 MB |\n| EL-GALEN | 3.24 GB | 807 MB | 440 MB |\n\nThe plan's target (≤ 2 GB and ≤ 2× el) is met on all three.\n\n**Most of the step from 3.24 GB was a leak, not the encoding.**\n- **The leak:** ksc-round pushed each round's new delta from its own body. An empty slop List names no arena, so list-push grew it in the store's never-freed arena instead of `na`. That was about 0.9 GB on EL-GALEN, every round's 96-byte facts plus abandoned growth buffers.\n- **The fix:** `delta-push`, which has `@alloc na`.\n- **The store itself:** on EL-GALEN, W's whole store is about 0.25 GB; the dedup set is 96 MB of 24-byte entries.\n\n**Answers are unchanged everywhere.**\n- Identical, rounds aside, to the pre-K7 engine on all 146 conformance reports and all 98 corpus fixtures.\n- Every class of OBI, GO and EL-GALEN matches.\n- All 21 gates pass; verify is 79/0/1.\n- All 14 mutants of the slice are caught: K7 ×8, cancellation ×2, ids ×4.\n\n**Codex review** found one defect: an element-scheme overflow bound applied to terms and roles. It is fixed with a per-scheme bound." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/982f9d9e-c500-48d1-b717-1eabdcaa1d58> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
