<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/b3773b27-f62b-4cc7-b91f-330e911f80ca> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Measured 2026-10-02 with `howl validate --profile el++`, reason phase:\n\n| | Before (phase W on one thread), W=4 | Now, W=1 | Now, W=4 | Now, W=8 |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| EL-GALEN | 5.0 s | 4.4 s | 1.9 s | 1.5 s |\n| GO | 1.2 s | 1.1 s | 0.56 s | 0.45 s |\n\nPeak memory is unchanged: EL-GALEN 0.81 GB, GO 0.62 GB.\n\n**Bench** (`make bench-el++`, W=4, informational):\n\n| | Before | Now |\n|---|---|---|\n| GO vs ELK | 2.3× | 1.1× |\n| EL-GALEN vs ELK | 15× | 6.0× |\n| OBI vs HermiT | — | 0.03× |\n\n**The remaining limit is the serial commit.** Before the commit was trimmed it was about 40% of the main thread's time. Committing pre-encoded facts with a seen-only check cut EL-GALEN at W=4 from 2.25 s to 1.87 s.\n\n**Checks:**\n- Answers are identical to the commit-on-derive engine on OBI, GO, EL-GALEN and RO.\n- Reports are byte-identical at W=1, 4 and 8.\n- `test-ksc-workers-agree` now compares every field at W ∈ {2,4,8} against W=1, at every cap 0..R, on all 33 fixtures.\n- `make determinism`: 5,856 el++ comparisons. ThreadSanitizer is clean. All 21 gates pass; verify is 81/0/1.\n\n**Codex review:** no race and no worker-count defect. Two findings, both fixed:\n- per-round bookkeeping and closure environments were allocated in the run arena;\n- the worker test compared too few fields." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/b3773b27-f62b-4cc7-b91f-330e911f80ca> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/b3773b27-f62b-4cc7-b91f-330e911f80ca> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-10-02T22:31:44.393923Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
