<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/b3f171a8-af1d-4080-8c39-f5b087fa885b> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Consequence> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/b3f171a8-af1d-4080-8c39-f5b087fa885b> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "The figure compared against ELK is prepare_ms + reason_ms, because ELK indexes inside its window" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/b3f171a8-af1d-4080-8c39-f5b087fa885b> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/b3f171a8-af1d-4080-8c39-f5b087fa885b> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "`reason_ms` counts saturation plus extraction, and the premise index is built in `prepare`. But the classification figure §12 M1 (c) compares against the oracle is `prepare_ms + reason_ms`, not `reason_ms` alone.\n\nThe earlier claim was that the index build mirrors \"ELK's indexing-at-load boundary\". That is wrong for ELK 0.6.0: ELK loads and indexes its axioms lazily, at the first query, so its indexing falls inside its classification window. `oracle bench` times the phases: on EL-GALEN at W = 4, create ~4 ms, consistent (load and index) ~70 ms, classify ~185 ms. Excluding HOWL's front end would therefore compare unlike boundaries in HOWL's favour.\n\nThese were corrected together in M1 slice 6:\n- the CLI's `print-timings` comment;\n- the `Prepared` comment in src/howl.slop;\n- SPEC §9." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/b3f171a8-af1d-4080-8c39-f5b087fa885b> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "superseded" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
