<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/b3fee881-1bf3-40bf-9de9-4f5d2842c6ff> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "The ladder's el++ citation is corrected from KKS12 to Krötzsch TR 3005" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/b3fee881-1bf3-40bf-9de9-4f5d2842c6ff> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/b3fee881-1bf3-40bf-9de9-4f5d2842c6ff> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "AD 355c704f's table cites \"KKS12 ELO\" as the `el++` calculus. That citation is wrong:\n- KKS12's Theorem 4 is proved for ELO only (⊤, ⊓, ∃, nominals), with no ⊥, role hierarchies, chains, ranges or Self.\n- The `el++` rung's combination is covered only by Krötzsch, KIT TR 3005 (2010), Theorem 2 (Ksc).\n\nSPEC §5's table and §16 references were corrected in PR #8. The ladder itself is unchanged: the same four rungs, the default `el`, and `el++` still PTIME and still the one rung incomparable with `horn-sriq` and `sriq`. The calculus decision is AD 42c907c9." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/b3fee881-1bf3-40bf-9de9-4f5d2842c6ff> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/b3fee881-1bf3-40bf-9de9-4f5d2842c6ff> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-10-01T02:55:40.0421Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/b3fee881-1bf3-40bf-9de9-4f5d2842c6ff> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "The ladder's el++ citation is corrected from KKS12 to Krötzsch TR 3005" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/b3fee881-1bf3-40bf-9de9-4f5d2842c6ff> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#resultsFrom> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/355c704f-3a87-4ed5-8ef3-907994d30ffe> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/b3fee881-1bf3-40bf-9de9-4f5d2842c6ff> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#resultsFrom> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/42c907c9-7083-42d8-b53e-0daff17089d8> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/b4e37a87-aad6-4119-ab5f-dab0a9fa2269> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Consequence> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/b4e37a87-aad6-4119-ab5f-dab0a9fa2269> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "A failed thread spawn is undetectable from SLOP until the thread module reports it" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/b4e37a87-aad6-4119-ab5f-dab0a9fa2269> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/b4e37a87-aad6-4119-ab5f-dab0a9fa2269> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "SLOP's `spawn` lowering ignores `pthread_create`'s return value. The thread struct's `id` and `result` are uninitialized arena memory (arenas are malloc'd, not zeroed). So if thread creation fails, `join` calls `pthread_join` on a garbage id, which is undefined behaviour, and returns a garbage result. HOWL's round would then merge an incomplete delta, and the report could depend on whether a spawn failed under resource pressure.\n\nHOWL cannot detect this soundly from SLOP: a sentinel return value could match by chance, and the join has already misbehaved. The fix belongs upstream: `spawn` must abort loudly, or return an error, when `pthread_create` fails. A crash then replaces a silently wrong report.\n\n**Mitigation in HOWL meanwhile:**\n- Worker arenas start at 1 MB, not 16, so a high `--workers` on a small frontier no longer asks for a gigabyte per round.\n- Workers are spawned only for non-empty shares, which lowers the resource pressure that makes a spawn fail.\n\nFound by the Codex review of M1 slice 5." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/b4e37a87-aad6-4119-ab5f-dab0a9fa2269> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "superseded" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/b4e37a87-aad6-4119-ab5f-dab0a9fa2269> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-09-27T18:18:07.423686Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/b4e37a87-aad6-4119-ab5f-dab0a9fa2269> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "A failed thread spawn is undetectable from SLOP until the thread module reports it" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/b4e37a87-aad6-4119-ab5f-dab0a9fa2269> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#isSupersededBy> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/b7178c76-47c6-4935-892a-2a45770ea66f> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/b4e37a87-aad6-4119-ab5f-dab0a9fa2269> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#resultsFrom> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/48b331ef-b073-490b-9785-e0afda7485d7> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/b7178c76-47c6-4935-892a-2a45770ea66f> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Consequence> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/b7178c76-47c6-4935-892a-2a45770ea66f> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "A failed thread spawn is undetectable from SLOP until the thread module reports it" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/b7178c76-47c6-4935-892a-2a45770ea66f> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/b7178c76-47c6-4935-892a-2a45770ea66f> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "SLOP's `spawn` lowering ignores `pthread_create`'s return value. The thread struct's `id` and `result` are uninitialized arena memory (arenas are malloc'd, not zeroed). So if thread creation fails, `join` calls `pthread_join` on a garbage id, which is undefined behaviour, and returns a garbage result. HOWL's round would then merge an incomplete delta, and the report could depend on whether a spawn failed under resource pressure.\n\nHOWL cannot detect this soundly from SLOP: a sentinel return value could match by chance, and the join has already misbehaved. The fix belongs upstream: `spawn` must abort loudly, or return an error, when `pthread_create` fails. A crash then replaces a silently wrong report. Tracked as slop-lang/slop#192, still open as of slop 0.3.0. SPEC §6.8 states the precondition: M1 (e) holds for runs where every spawn succeeds.\n\n**Mitigation in HOWL meanwhile:**\n- Worker arenas start at 1 MB, not 16, so a high `--workers` on a small frontier no longer asks for a gigabyte per round.\n- Workers are spawned only for non-empty shares, which lowers the resource pressure that makes a spawn fail.\n\nFound by the Codex review of M1 slice 5." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/b7178c76-47c6-4935-892a-2a45770ea66f> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
