<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/bcb0ef2f-067c-46a3-bc75-23cb768b11cf> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Consequence> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/bcb0ef2f-067c-46a3-bc75-23cb768b11cf> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Only el built: out-of-v0 input is inconclusive; later, auto (not the default) selects v1" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/bcb0ef2f-067c-46a3-bc75-23cb768b11cf> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/bcb0ef2f-067c-46a3-bc75-23cb768b11cf> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "With only `el` built, an ontology outside the v0 language has nothing to escalate to, so the run is inconclusive and never 'coherent'. Once `horn-sriq` (v1) exists, an ontology using inverses or functionality and otherwise inside Horn-SRIQ must be run there by `auto` rather than reported inconclusive. The DEFAULT selection stays `explicit el` (AD 355c704f), so a default run still reports such an ontology inconclusive, listing every omission; the caller opts into `auto` or names the rung." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/bcb0ef2f-067c-46a3-bc75-23cb768b11cf> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
