<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/cf4cb422-0636-4a6c-96d8-10fa18007713> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "el++ is selectable: --profile el++, and auto chooses between el and el++" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/cf4cb422-0636-4a6c-96d8-10fa18007713> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/cf4cb422-0636-4a6c-96d8-10fa18007713> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Slice 6c, 2026-10-02.\n\n**What changed.**\n- `profile-implemented` admits `el` and `el++`; horn-sriq and sriq are still refused as `unavailable`.\n- `select-profile` now leaves `auto` unresolved (none), since auto depends on the ontology.\n- **`choose-auto`** (src/select.slop, three proved posts) implements AD 3eacfa8e's rule over the two built rungs: `el` when nothing is out of el's profile, else the rung with fewer logical axioms out of profile, ties to `el`.\n- `prepare-decoded` resolves `auto` by gating under `el` and, only if el omits something, under `el++`, in a scratch arena. It counts out-of-profile omissions only; unresolved imports and missing declarations are rung-invariant. Only the winner is prepared, and the report's profile line names it.\n- **Measured choices:**\n\n  | Fixture | el omits | el++ omits | auto picks |\n  |---|---|---|---|\n  | litmus | 0 | 0 | el |\n  | has-self | 1 | 0 | el++ |\n  | union | 1 | 1 | el |\n  | nominals | 2 | 1 | el++ |\n  | property-characteristics | 6 | 5 | el++ |\n\n- **Fixtures.** has-self, equality and builtin-roles moved from out-of-profile/ to corpus/fixtures/el++/. The el++ engine's inline test fixtures became files there (ksc-00…ksc-32), one source for make test and the coming oracle differential.\n- **Goldens.** A new el++ golden set covers el++/ and v0/ fixtures under `--profile el++`, plus report hashes for RO, OBI, GO and EL-GALEN. Every v0 report is identical under el and el++, profile and rounds aside.\n- **Acceptance** gains el++, auto and --strict cases.\n\n**Rust is not wired.** The crate's `classify` stays NotImplemented. Binding it needs a slop-rdf-sys release that vendors slop-rdf ≥ 73091e0 (OWL 2 reserved vocab): 14 HOWL modules, including the decoder and the el++ engine, cannot link against slop-rdf-sys v0.2.1. rust/build.rs documents this.\n\n**Checks.** All 21 gates pass; verify is 80/0/1; examples 76. Six select mutants are refuted by their contracts. Codex: no defect in auto, strict, profile reporting or arena lifetimes; the Rust doc table's \"Built\" column was clarified to mean the engine." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
