<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/d98a51ef-296a-4d41-a7b3-ee4592486c0b> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "HOWL's peak memory against ELK and HermiT after the memory work" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/d98a51ef-296a-4d41-a7b3-ee4592486c0b> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/d98a51ef-296a-4d41-a7b3-ee4592486c0b> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Peak RSS of one full run, parse to report, W = 4, on an Apple M3 Ultra. Oracles are measured at their default 32 GB heap, and at the smallest heap that still reproduces the certified entailments (bisected to within 10%).\n\n| Entry | HOWL | HOWL (MallocLargeCache=0) | Oracle, 32 GB heap | Oracle, smallest heap |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| GO | 2.6 GB | 1.7 GB | ELK 4.1–7.6 GB | ELK 0.9 GB (0.61 GB heap) |\n| EL-GALEN | 2.1 GB | 1.1 GB | ELK 1.9 GB | ELK 0.43 GB (0.21 GB heap) |\n| OBI | 0.58 GB | 0.29 GB | HermiT 1.4 GB | HermiT 0.24 GB (59 MB heap) |\n| RO | 33 MB | 32 MB | HermiT 0.36 GB | HermiT 0.23 GB (67 MB heap) |\n\n**Against the oracles as they are normally configured,** HOWL uses less on every entry.\n\n**Against what the oracles minimally need,** HOWL uses 1.2–4.8× more on the large ontologies, or 1.2–2.6× once the allocator returns freed memory. It uses less on small ones, where the JVM's own baseline of about 0.2 GB dominates.\n\n**Where the remaining gap sits:**\n- the per-element cost of slop's Map and Set, roughly 50–200 B an entry against a 4 B JVM reference;\n- macOS keeping freed arena blocks resident. The slop arena fix for that was requested on 2026-09-29.\n\nBench at the same point: GO 1.31× and EL-GALEN 3.54× ELK, so M1 (c) is met." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
