<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/de5e1d70-49d7-4165-912d-98bce441b096> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Step A benchmark: GO 16.6x and EL-GALEN 22.4x ELK, down from 19.2x and 30.1x" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/de5e1d70-49d7-4165-912d-98bce441b096> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/de5e1d70-49d7-4165-912d-98bce441b096> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "`make bench` after M1 slice 6b step A (bench/results.txt; W = 4; median of 5 after 1 warm-up; every run reproduced the certified report):\n\n| Entry | Oracle | HOWL classify | Oracle classify | Ratio (S6a) |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| GO | ELK | 9,982 ms (reason 2,128; peak 19 GB) | 601 ms | **16.61×** (19.20×) |\n| EL-GALEN | ELK | 8,983 ms (reason 7,015; peak 9 GB, was 14 GB) | 402 ms | **22.35×** (30.08×) |\n| OBI | HermiT | 730 ms | 568 ms | 1.29× (1.31×), reported |\n| RO | HermiT | 57 ms | 180 ms | 0.32× (0.33×), reported |\n\n**Load.** The machine was busy during this run (load average 4.2 → 6.5, from other sessions' agents), and ELK's own EL-GALEN time rose from S6a's 318 ms to 402 ms. Quiet single runs put HOWL's EL-GALEN reasoning at ~5.1 s at W = 4. The verdict (not met) holds either way.\n\n**Where the time goes now:**\n- **Reasoning.** Single-threaded EL-GALEN samples halved (19,119 → 9,044). Node/RoleId hash and equality are still ~45% of reasoning. `round-commit`, which is serial at the barrier, is now ~23%, and it caps the speedup from workers.\n- **GO's classify time** is dominated by the single-threaded front end: `prepare` ~7 s, most of it slop-rdf's four-index build. That is Step B's target.\n- **Hashing** is Step C's target, and the SLOP map PR's." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
