<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/dfaa7fc2-018b-4a71-b849-492a67a40c5a> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Consequence> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/dfaa7fc2-018b-4a71-b849-492a67a40c5a> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "BFO-core: HOWL's taxonomy equals HermiT's; the disjunctive residue matters for ABox validation" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/dfaa7fc2-018b-4a71-b849-492a67a40c5a> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/dfaa7fc2-018b-4a71-b849-492a67a40c5a> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Measured 2026-09-30 on BFO-core (growl/cli/tests/fixtures/bfo-core.ttl) with HermiT 1.4.5 through oracle/ and HOWL at the memory_work head. HOWL omits 76 axioms (verdict inconclusive), yet its 194 subsumptions, 0 unsatisfiable classes and 'consistent' are IDENTICAL to HermiT's.\n\n**The 76 omissions, by what they need:**\n| Needs | Axioms | Examples |\n|---|---|---|\n| Inverse roles, functionality (Horn-SHIQ) | 24 | 17 InverseObjectProperties, 6 functional, 1 inverse-functional |\n| Universal on the right (Horn with inverses) | 21 | A ⊑ ∀r.B |\n| Negation in a domain/range conjunct (Horn: disjointness) | 9 | domain(r) = C ⊓ ¬D |\n| Disjunction in positive position (non-Horn) | 22 | domain/range = A ⊔ B; A ⊑ ∀r.(B ⊔ C) |\n\n**Where the disjunctive residue matters:** an ABox probe (a process as the subject of BFO_0000056 'participates in', whose domain is a union of continuant kinds) is inconsistent under HermiT; HOWL reports inconclusive (safe, but misses it). Adding the union domain's Horn weakening (domain ⊑ BFO_0000002 continuant, the members' common named subsumer; entailed by the union) makes HOWL report inconsistent / incoherent.\n\n**Implication:** BFO does not need full DL. A path: Horn-SHIQ core (inverses, functional, ∀ on the right) + sound Horn weakening of positive disjunctions to their least common named subsumer (violation detection, still inconclusive) + upper-bound certification (a strengthened Horn theory that is coherent certifies coherent, PAGOdA-style). Complete reasoning over the residue needs a consequence-based ALCHI/SHIF calculus (Simančík-Kazakov-Horrocks; Sequoia), which is still deterministic saturation, not tableau search. CCO not yet measured (not vendored)." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/dfaa7fc2-018b-4a71-b849-492a67a40c5a> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
