<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/e9f949af-a048-41cd-8b57-1f0f0ecff8c4> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Evidence beside the proof: seven ABox lemma fixtures (super-role range, complex range filler, domain on an asserted edge, mixed and n-ary chains over individuals, owl:Nothing(a), complex class assertion), all diff-clean against HermiT; make abox-fuzz: 400 of 400 generated v0 ontologies with ABoxes match HermiT (169 inconsistent). Mutations caught by both fixtures and fuzz: range seeds dropped; direct ranges only; asserted edges routed through ∃ (the fuzzer needed a bias toward two roles' disjoint ranges meeting at one individual before it caught that one). Right-associated chain decomposition was dropped as a mutation: it changes no answer, only the paper's literal restriction." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/ee1a7a87-9248-4cf8-ab2e-89abf2c6c849> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Consequence> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/ee1a7a87-9248-4cf8-ab2e-89abf2c6c849> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "The census fixes regenerated OBI's projection and exposed stale MANIFEST figures" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/ee1a7a87-9248-4cf8-ab2e-89abf2c6c849> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/ee1a7a87-9248-4cf8-ab2e-89abf2c6c849> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "The conformance work brought census.py level with HOWL's gate in four places:\n- class assertions over blank-node class expressions;\n- `someValuesFrom` on a data property, including the built-in data properties;\n- `owl:Annotation` nodes;\n- `owl:AllDisjointClasses`.\n\n**OBI.** Five data-property `someValuesFrom` axioms had been counted as in v0. The pinned OBI projection kept them, so HOWL would have omitted them from \"projected\" OBI in S4. OBI was regenerated: 379 → 384 axioms and 5,828 → 5,848 triples removed, with the ground-triple hash unchanged. RO and GO did not move.\n\n**RO.** The MANIFEST's in_v0/out_of_profile for RO were already stale before this work (1465/518 against the census's 1463/520), and nothing checked them. `project.py --verify` now compares every MANIFEST figure (in_v0, out_of_profile, and the three projection_removes counts) with the census and fails on any difference. Restoring RO's stale figure makes it fail.\n\nThis is the census-versus-gate drift S4's reconciliation exists to close, surfacing early." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/ee1a7a87-9248-4cf8-ab2e-89abf2c6c849> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/ee1a7a87-9248-4cf8-ab2e-89abf2c6c849> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-09-27T03:01:37.653571Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/ee1a7a87-9248-4cf8-ab2e-89abf2c6c849> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "The census fixes regenerated OBI's projection and exposed stale MANIFEST figures" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/ee1a7a87-9248-4cf8-ab2e-89abf2c6c849> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#resultsFrom> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/e613b055-386a-47e2-8748-192cc59dd02d> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/efaaa568-e8df-47cf-abe9-ab455d8826de> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Consequence> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/efaaa568-e8df-47cf-abe9-ab455d8826de> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "K6's shared saturation takes EL-GALEN from ~11.5 h to 8.7 s; its 10.3 GB peak is the open cost" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/efaaa568-e8df-47cf-abe9-ab455d8826de> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/efaaa568-e8df-47cf-abe9-ab455d8826de> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Slice 5b's engine (PR #15) implements K6. Phase W saturates every queried class and the individuals at once. Safe classes are answered from W; only unsafe classes run over G ∪ W_S. Classes and roles enter as dense ids, and rules (6)–(8) join through two-level partner maps. Reasoning time, with G and W single-threaded:\n- **OBI:** 0.16 s for all 5,241 classes (156 unsafe), down from 1.6 s.\n- **GO:** 1.2 s (all classes safe), down from ~31 s projected.\n- **EL-GALEN:** 8.7 s (all safe), down from ~11.5 h projected.\n\n**Answers.** Every class's answers equal the K2-only engine's on OBI and GO. The one exception is owl:Nothing's own subsumer list: W completes it, while a run flagged at ⊥ stops early (K3).\n\n**Speed came mostly from partner joins.** Each step was measured separately:\n- dense names took GO from 29 s to 20 s;\n- partner joins then took it from 20 s to 1.2 s;\n- partner joins took EL-GALEN from 16 s to 8.7 s.\n\n**Memory is the open cost: EL-GALEN peaks at 10.3 GB.**\n- W holds 10.3M facts, 8.4M of them triples.\n- Each fact is stored by value in the dedup set and the indexes.\n- Rule (13) materialises every triple under each super-role.\n- `el` holds the same ontology in under 1 GB by reading the role hierarchy through its closure. Doing that for el++ needs its own argument, and SPEC §5.4 says so." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/efaaa568-e8df-47cf-abe9-ab455d8826de> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/efaaa568-e8df-47cf-abe9-ab455d8826de> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-10-02T01:43:29.782469Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/efaaa568-e8df-47cf-abe9-ab455d8826de> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "K6's shared saturation takes EL-GALEN from ~11.5 h to 8.7 s; its 10.3 GB peak is the open cost" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/efaaa568-e8df-47cf-abe9-ab455d8826de> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#resultsFrom> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/5570d76e-8682-4300-965e-025884269d65> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/f313a16e-04d7-411b-ad7d-6120e053b844> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Consequence> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/f313a16e-04d7-411b-ad7d-6120e053b844> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "slop's OS-mapped arena blocks take GO to 0.91 GB, level with ELK's minimum" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/f313a16e-04d7-411b-ad7d-6120e053b844> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/f313a16e-04d7-411b-ad7d-6120e053b844> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "HOWL was regenerated from slop main 18a5f44. slop #235 maps big arena blocks from the OS, so freeing an arena now returns its memory; macOS's malloc had kept freed large blocks resident. This resolves Lesson adeb3806. Every report is unchanged, all gates pass, and verify reports 35 verified / 0 failed / 1 unknown.\n\n**Peak memory** (default allocator; now equal to the earlier MallocLargeCache=0 figures):\n\n| | before | now | oracle's smallest workable heap |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| GO | 1,814 MB | 913 MB | ELK 0.9 GB |\n| EL-GALEN | 1,537 MB | 624 MB | ELK 0.43 GB |\n| OBI | 407 MB | 236 MB | HermiT 0.24 GB |\n| RO | 29 MB | 23 MB | HermiT 0.23 GB |\n\nSince M1, GO has gone from 7.9 GB to 0.91 GB, an 8.7× reduction.\n\n**Bench** (clean run, load 2.8 → 4.3): M1 (c) met. GO is 0.77× (444 ms vs ELK 575) and EL-GALEN 2.60× (910 vs 350). ELK ran slower than in earlier sessions; against those medians the figures are about 1.0× and 3.2×. Returning memory costs HOWL a little time: GO's classification went from 389 to 444 ms, because later rounds touch fresh pages.\n\n**The peak is now the parse** on every entry: GO reaches 851 MB during the parse. slop-rdf's parser holds every term occurrence's strings until the parse ends, so a per-statement scratch arena there is the remaining lever.\n\nAn earlier bench attempt overlapped a still-running bench from a killed job; its figures were discarded and the bench re-run alone." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/f313a16e-04d7-411b-ad7d-6120e053b844> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "superseded" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/f313a16e-04d7-411b-ad7d-6120e053b844> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-09-30T03:11:31.151651Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/f313a16e-04d7-411b-ad7d-6120e053b844> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "slop's OS-mapped arena blocks take GO to 0.91 GB, level with ELK's minimum" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/f313a16e-04d7-411b-ad7d-6120e053b844> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#isSupersededBy> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/925ded84-3212-41b0-8b6e-37ed8b72805e> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/f313a16e-04d7-411b-ad7d-6120e053b844> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#resultsFrom> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/0a305284-0b59-47e0-ba53-e00b48012cba> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/f507f445-bfc4-4b03-b281-67752e7e1e6c> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Consequence> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/f507f445-bfc4-4b03-b281-67752e7e1e6c> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "slop's map work takes the benchmark to GO 9.5x and EL-GALEN 12.3x ELK, with every report unchanged" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/f507f445-bfc4-4b03-b281-67752e7e1e6c> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/f507f445-bfc4-4b03-b281-67752e7e1e6c> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "HOWL was regenerated from slop main 78e4209 (slop-lang/slop#205, \"map-perf\"). The changes:\n- `slop_map` entries store their hash;\n- growth reuses the stored hash and no longer re-copies keys;\n- capacity is a power of two, masked;\n- strings hash a word at a time;\n- string equality checks identity first;\n- `(Option T)` key fields hash and compare by content;\n- `set-len` and `map-len` are new.\n\n**Correctness.** Every gate passed, with no report changed: goldens byte-identical, including the RO/OBI/GO/EL-GALEN report hashes, and determinism identical on fixtures and corpus. Map and Set iteration order changed with the hash functions and reached no report. Step 0 (Lesson c974f9a6) was the prerequisite.\n\n**Literals.** slop-rdf's Literal datatype and lang are now hashed and compared by content rather than as raw bytes, which had included pointers and padding.\n\n**`set-len`.** It replaces `subsumer-count`'s `c-inline` in the CR2/CR4 smaller-side choice (AD 3e6b52c2). The generated C is the same `->len` read.\n\n**Bench** (bench/results.txt, load 2.9–3.2):\n\n| Entry | HOWL classify | Oracle | Ratio |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| GO | 4,248 ms (reason 954) | ELK 446 ms | **9.52×** |\n| EL-GALEN | 3,343 ms (reason 2,569) | ELK 273 ms | **12.25×** |\n| OBI | 347 ms | HermiT 510 ms | 0.68× |\n| RO | 34 ms | HermiT 159 ms | 0.21× |\n\nThe progression: S6a 19.2× / 30.1× → step A 16.6× / 22.4× (loaded run) → now.\n\n**Measurement caveat.** HOWL's timings rise across back-to-back runs. Each EL-GALEN run allocates ~9 GB, and the next run appears to pay while the OS reclaims the previous process's memory. The oracle's runs share one JVM and don't pay this. The bias is against HOWL, the safe direction for a gate, but it makes HOWL's medians pessimistic.\n\n**Remaining gap to 5×:**\n- GO's single-threaded front end, ~3 s of 4.2 s, mostly slop-rdf's four-index store. That is Step B.\n- IRI hashing and comparison in reasoning. That is Step C." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
