<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/6142429c-250e-4617-8e91-5bfea4574925> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/6142429c-250e-4617-8e91-5bfea4574925> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "HOWL v0 accepts exactly ELH⊥R+ plus domain and range axioms, plus ABox assertions, plus ¬E (E in that language) as the whole filler or a top-level conjunct of a superclass, domain or range. The complement is REWRITTEN BEFORE THE GATE into ⊥ GCIs with no fresh names:\n- C ⊑ P ⊓ ¬E ⇒ C ⊑ P, C ⊓ E ⊑ ⊥\n- dom(r) ⊑ P ⊓ ¬E ⇒ dom(r) ⊑ P, ∃r.⊤ ⊓ E ⊑ ⊥\n- ran(r) ⊑ P ⊓ ¬E ⇒ ran(r) ⊑ P, ∃r.E ⊑ ⊥\n\nIt rewrites whole axioms or nothing, so an axiom with any piece out of profile is omitted as written. Every gate condition, the range/composition condition included, judges the rewritten theory. The logic is unchanged, and ¬ anywhere else stays out of profile. Ranges are handled by the PUBLISHED ELIMINATION CONSTRUCTION during normalization, never by a new completion rule. The rule set is exactly CR1–CR7 from the cited CEL formulation.\n\nRANGES: IN, BY ELIMINATION. Domain(r) ⊑ C is ∃r.⊤ ⊑ C. Range uses the X_{r,D} rewrite from \"Pushing the EL Envelope FURTHER\" (OWLED 2008), with ran_T computed over the TOLD role hierarchy, and X_{r,D} is SHARED per (r,D). Complex range fillers are normalized to a name first, so NormAxiom needs no range constructor. Asserted edges need HOWL's own extension: installing r(a,b) seeds every A in ran_T(r) into S(individual(b)). The admissibility condition (every range imposed on a composed role t is also imposed on the chain's last role, through the told hierarchy on both sides) is a precondition of the construction, so it lives in the gate. After the negation rewrite, only positive ranges are ranges.\n\nNOMINALS: OUT. They would change the data model rather than extend it.\n\nFOUR DISJOINT DISPOSITIONS, a total function over RawAxiom:\n- In-profile (classified).\n- Inert (annotation vocabulary).\n- Consumed (declaration triples: read, but produce no axiom).\n- Out-of-profile (enumerated in the report, verdict inconclusive).\nInertness is STRUCTURAL, not an IRI whitelist.\n\nEvidence: SPEC.md §5.2 (the exact v0 language, the negation rewrite, the elimination block, the disposition tables), §5.3 L0, §6.3, §6.4." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
