<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/351e4c85-8221-400b-ad97-ffc72f8d83ee> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "The slop verify boundary: expression shape, not claim meaning" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/351e4c85-8221-400b-ad97-ffc72f8d83ee> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#isSupersededBy> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/772eff39-94f7-4692-92ea-23f39da47e50> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/351e4c85-8221-400b-ad97-ffc72f8d83ee> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#learnedFrom> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/85e6f9fb-40ea-497b-b689-3074f1a4ad52> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/351e4c85-8221-400b-ad97-ffc72f8d83ee> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#supersedes> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/bb5a926e-bd43-4a54-8e86-bac9dbfd630f> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/3638a9b5-ab3c-4b47-965f-407223954c17> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Lesson> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/3638a9b5-ab3c-4b47-965f-407223954c17> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "A key renderer that drops a variant's payload merges distinct objects" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/3638a9b5-ab3c-4b47-965f-407223954c17> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/3638a9b5-ab3c-4b47-965f-407223954c17> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "normalize.slop's render-node-name rendered EVERY fresh-node as the constant \"_:fresh\", so range-elim-key gave X_{r,D} the same key for every non-named filler D on role r. All of r's complex fillers collapsed into one X that inherited every filler's subsumers; disjoint subsumers put ⊥ into X and from there into every class using ∃r with a complex filler.\n\nEvidence: OBI (118k triples, consistent) reported INCOHERENT/inconsistent with 2137 false unsatisfiable classes once the ABox was removed. Bisection: removing ranges OR disjointness cleared it; removing domains or the ABox did not. Minimal repro: C1 ⊑ ∃r.(P⊓Q), C2 ⊑ ∃r.(U⊓V), Disjoint(P,U), range(r)=R → INCOHERENT; without the range → coherent. Keying fresh fillers by id fixed the repro and OBI (exit 2, 0 unsatisfiable, 38,681 subsumptions — identical to the no-range variant) and cut OBI's run from 8 min to 168 s. All 69 tests and 6 acceptance fixtures passed BOTH before and after the fix: no fixture puts a complex filler on a ranged role.\n\nRule: a function that renders a canonical KEY must be injective over what it keys — every variant's payload appears in the output, never a placeholder constant. A display renderer (owl2.slop render-node, which also prints \"_:fresh-node\") is not a key renderer, and must not be reused as one. When a key collapses, the symptom is not a crash but a SHARED fresh symbol: over-derivation, which in a DL reasoner is unsoundness." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/3638a9b5-ab3c-4b47-965f-407223954c17> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "superseded" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/3638a9b5-ab3c-4b47-965f-407223954c17> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-09-14T06:47:18.695952Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/3638a9b5-ab3c-4b47-965f-407223954c17> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "A key renderer that drops a variant's payload merges distinct objects" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/3638a9b5-ab3c-4b47-965f-407223954c17> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#isSupersededBy> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/a9a014e2-7e90-430f-bb23-dbc10958a82d> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/3a45b0a7-cf28-45d8-abc4-08494d91b064> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Lesson> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/3a45b0a7-cf28-45d8-abc4-08494d91b064> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Check a cited completeness result: its later literature, and its logic" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/3a45b0a7-cf28-45d8-abc4-08494d91b064> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/3a45b0a7-cf28-45d8-abc4-08494d91b064> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "A completeness citation can fail in two ways, and each needs its own check.\n\n**1. Later work can refute it.** A published completeness lemma can be refuted by later work, so check what followed before citing it. SPEC §5.3 cited BBL05 (IJCAI 2005) Lemma 3 for completeness with nominals. It passed four adversarial reviews and the owner's acceptance, yet KKS12 (KR 2012) had shown that claim false for nominals. It surfaced only when a literature agent, asked about profile rungs, read the follow-up papers.\n\n**2. Its logic may not cover the combination.** A completeness theorem covers its own logic and nothing more, even when the paper says the results \"can be applied to other logics\". The profile ladder (AD 355c704f) cited KKS12 for the `el++` rung, but KKS12's Theorem 4 is proved for ELO only: no ⊥, role hierarchies, chains, ranges or Self. The one proof covering the rung's combination is Krötzsch TR 3005 Theorem 2 (AD 42c907c9). It surfaced only when the `el++` plan asked which proof covers the whole combination.\n\n**Pattern:** a lemma or theorem cited from the paper that introduced a calculus is trusted as stated and as broad as the topic. Reviewers check the reduction against that paper's text, not against later errata or the theorem's stated logic, so every check passes.\n\n**Rule:** before citing a completeness or soundness result:\n- **(a) Read what followed it.** Search for later work that cites it, especially from the same authors or the same tool line (for example ELK's papers for CEL/EL++).\n- **(b) Check its logic against the construct list.** Compare the logic the theorem is stated for, construct by construct, against EVERY construct the citing rung accepts. A remark that the result extends to other features is not a proof.\n\nRecord both checks in the citing section. Where a result is disputed or narrower, use only the undisputed, covered part, as §5.3 does (soundness from Lemma 3, completeness from a direct canonical model), or find the proof that covers the combination." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/3a45b0a7-cf28-45d8-abc4-08494d91b064> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
