<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/772eff39-94f7-4692-92ea-23f39da47e50> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#isSupersededBy> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/1d0011c7-4851-4d51-b36a-aa240eb619b8> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/772eff39-94f7-4692-92ea-23f39da47e50> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#learnedFrom> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/85e6f9fb-40ea-497b-b689-3074f1a4ad52> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/772eff39-94f7-4692-92ea-23f39da47e50> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#supersedes> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/351e4c85-8221-400b-ad97-ffc72f8d83ee> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/7cd9a031-04d3-4f18-a179-65e11d5cdbe3> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Lesson> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/7cd9a031-04d3-4f18-a179-65e11d5cdbe3> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "An empty slop List grows in the pushing function's arena, not the one it was made in" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/7cd9a031-04d3-4f18-a179-65e11d5cdbe3> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/7cd9a031-04d3-4f18-a179-65e11d5cdbe3> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "**The trap.** `(list-new na T)` returns `{NULL, 0, 0}`, which names no arena. `list-push` grows a list in the arena of the function doing the push: its @alloc arena, the first Arena parameter. So `ksc-round` (@alloc arena) pushed its next delta into the store's never-freed arena. Every round's 96-byte facts, and every growth buffer they abandoned, leaked: about 0.9 GB on EL-GALEN, from slice 5 until 2026-10-02.\n\n**How it hid.** The code comment said the delta was \"in `na`\", and nothing measured it. It was found only by attributing arena growth per call.\n\n**Rule.**\n- To grow a list in a scratch arena, push from a helper whose @alloc is that arena (`delta-push`). Don't rely on where the list was created.\n- When memory is far above what the live data explains, measure arena *used* bytes (sum of block offsets) per call site; don't reason about it.\n- macOS resident size is unreliable for this: idle pages get compressed. ru_maxrss gives the peak, arena offsets give the cause." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/7cd9a031-04d3-4f18-a179-65e11d5cdbe3> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "deprecated" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/7cd9a031-04d3-4f18-a179-65e11d5cdbe3> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasRationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/bbc89446-ab5c-4a9f-bc38-767331f3e725> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/7cd9a031-04d3-4f18-a179-65e11d5cdbe3> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-10-02T05:12:40.57448Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/7cd9a031-04d3-4f18-a179-65e11d5cdbe3> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "An empty slop List grows in the pushing function's arena, not the one it was made in" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/7cd9a031-04d3-4f18-a179-65e11d5cdbe3> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#learnedFrom> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/7910309f-70ea-4f71-a3bf-8e4d753c05b2> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/9443f5d9-0945-4fb6-aea0-6ef477869ece> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Lesson> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/9443f5d9-0945-4fb6-aea0-6ef477869ece> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Seed the delta, not the store — semi-naive bootstrap" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/9443f5d9-0945-4fb6-aea0-6ef477869ece> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/9443f5d9-0945-4fb6-aea0-6ef477869ece> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "In a semi-naive fixpoint, initial facts must be placed in the INITIAL DELTA, not written directly into the fact store. Writing them into the store leaves every work queue empty, so the driver reaches its termination condition before firing a single rule.\n\nThe instance: HOWL initializes S(N) = {N, ⊤} for every context. A draft specified this as seeding the `subsumers` set. Since rules fire only on facts arriving in Δₙ, and `active` tracks contexts with non-empty queues, `active` would be empty at round 0 — the driver reports `fixpoint`, and CR1 through CR3 never process N or ⊤ at all. Correct form is S₋₁ := ∅ with Δ₀(N) := { derived-sub(N), derived-sub(⊤) }, so round 0 forms S₀ = ∅ ∪ Δ₀ and joins against it, with every context starting active.\n\nWhy this one is especially dangerous rather than merely wrong: the failure is not a crash or a missing conclusion in an edge case. The run terminates instantly, reports `fixpoint` with empty coverage omissions — i.e. COMPLETE — and returns an empty classification. Under the verdict rule that is a clean \"coherent\" verdict. Sound, catastrophically incomplete, and indistinguishable from success at every interface.\n\nIt is also nearly untestable by accident. Any fixture with ordinary axioms generates deltas through other paths and masks the bug. The test that catches it must have the initial seed as its ONLY enabling premise — e.g. `⊤ ⊑ C` over a single otherwise-axiom-free class, where the answer depends entirely on ⊤ ∈ Δ₀ reaching CR1.\n\nGeneralizes to any delta-driven fixpoint including GROWL's: whenever a design says \"the state is initialized to X\", ask whether X is visible to the rules, which for semi-naive evaluation means asking whether X is in a delta. Related to [[semi-naive-rounds-must-join-the-delta-against-a-snapshot-that-includes-itself]]. Captured 2026-08-12." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
