<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/bbd185cd-89f4-44c6-a362-fd423e39947d> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#isSupersededBy> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/bb5a926e-bd43-4a54-8e86-bac9dbfd630f> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/bbd185cd-89f4-44c6-a362-fd423e39947d> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#learnedFrom> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/85e6f9fb-40ea-497b-b689-3074f1a4ad52> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/bc1c828b-e745-404f-a5bc-652a001da9f9> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Lesson> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/bc1c828b-e745-404f-a5bc-652a001da9f9> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "A coverage table tracks progress toward a target, not a claim of reaching it" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/bc1c828b-e745-404f-a5bc-652a001da9f9> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/bc1c828b-e745-404f-a5bc-652a001da9f9> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "When asked for a table of \"adherence\" to a target language (EL++), build a progress tracker toward that target — do not argue against a conformance claim the user never made.\n\nPattern: the user asked \"Shall we add a table to the README detailing HOWL's adherence [to EL++]?\" I read it as a proposal to claim HOWL is EL++, spent the answer rebutting that (\"a README saying so would overclaim\"), and built a table of what v0 accepts and rejects. The user corrected: the table is to track where HOWL is on its way to EL++. The construct-by-construct discipline was right (Constraint: expressivity is claimed construct-by-construct, never by label); the framing was wrong.\n\nRule: before rebutting a premise, check whether the premise is actually being asserted. For a coverage/adherence table, organize rows by the TARGET's constructs (both the DL and its W3C profile where they differ), with a status column (done / not yet / non-goal), what each open row takes, and whether any milestone schedules it — so the table measures distance, not just the current language." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/bc1c828b-e745-404f-a5bc-652a001da9f9> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/bc1c828b-e745-404f-a5bc-652a001da9f9> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-09-14T05:26:55.362427Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/bc1c828b-e745-404f-a5bc-652a001da9f9> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "A coverage table tracks progress toward a target, not a claim of reaching it" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/c75e8926-cbe2-41f2-b825-fe3e142a1940> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Lesson> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/c75e8926-cbe2-41f2-b825-fe3e142a1940> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "A slop collection grows in the arena it was made in; cross-thread growth names :arena" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/c75e8926-cbe2-41f2-b825-fe3e142a1940> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/c75e8926-cbe2-41f2-b825-fe3e142a1940> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "**The rule since slop #278 (merged 2026-10-03, df93c3a):**\n- `list-new`, `map-new` and `set-new` record their arena.\n- `list-push`, `map-put` and `set-put` grow the collection in that recorded arena, whatever arena is in scope at the push.\n- A put can name another arena with `:arena a`.\n- `spawn` allocates a capturing closure's environment in the arena it is given.\n\n**Where `:arena` is REQUIRED.** It is needed when a thread grows a collection that another thread made, so that each thread grows in an arena of its own. In HOWL:\n- **el's parallel commit (src/saturate.slop):** committers grow the run's store sets and maps, and the coordinator's `qs.by-node` map. Those puts carry `:arena arena`, the committer's own arena.\n- **What happens without it:** `make test-tsan` reports a race in `slop_map_put` from `commit-entry`. Verified 2026-10-03 by removing the `qs.by-node` `:arena`.\n\n**What #278 retired.** The old rule picked a variable named `arena`, else the innermost `let`-bound arena. That put an el++ worker's results in an arena emptied after every fact, and a round's lists in a worker's arena. el++'s steering helpers (`delta-push`, `cfact-push`, `put-chunk`) are removed, because the collections now grow where they were made.\n\n**Rule:**\n- create a collection in the arena it should live in;\n- name `:arena` only for cross-thread growth;\n- confirm with `make test-asan` and `make test-tsan`." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/c75e8926-cbe2-41f2-b825-fe3e142a1940> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/c75e8926-cbe2-41f2-b825-fe3e142a1940> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasRationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/47fb5b17-98af-4fd5-94da-94837024c314> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
