<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/c974f9a6-2168-47b8-a838-2edd3152d641> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Lesson> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/c974f9a6-2168-47b8-a838-2edd3152d641> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "An index's iteration order is hash order: never let it decide what a report says" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/c974f9a6-2168-47b8-a838-2edd3152d641> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/c974f9a6-2168-47b8-a838-2edd3152d641> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "A lookup structure answers \"which\" correctly, but the order it answers in is hash-bucket order, a function of the hash function and the table's growth history, not of the input. Iterating a Set, or the list an index query returns, is only safe where the result is consumed as a set. Anywhere order reaches output (list order, last-writer-wins, first-found), take the order from the input (document order) or from a canonical sort.\n\n**The instance (M1 slice 6b step 0).**\n- **The leak.** `stage0-header` took the owl:Axiom subjects from `indexed-graph-subjects`, and that order reached two places:\n  - the order rebuilt reified triples join the list;\n  - which of several malformed reifications' fault messages is reported, because the loop was last-writer-wins.\n- **Why it hid.** It was deterministic under one hash function, so every run agreed, and nothing was caught until a planned SLOP runtime change (a new string hash) made the latent dependency visible on paper.\n- **The fix.** `typed-subjects-in-order` walks the triple list, and `test-stage0-fault-follows-the-document` flips the fault when the triples are reversed. That test was red on the hash-ordered code.\n\n**Rule.** When a runtime change alters hashing, audit every loop over a Set, a Map, or an index result for order-sensitive consumers *before* the change lands, not after the goldens move. The goldens cannot catch a fault message, because a fault gives exit 3 with no report." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/c974f9a6-2168-47b8-a838-2edd3152d641> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/c974f9a6-2168-47b8-a838-2edd3152d641> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-09-28T17:18:38.975887Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
