<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/d03dea42-7083-461f-833a-5acca0c08843> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Lesson> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/d03dea42-7083-461f-833a-5acca0c08843> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "IRIs come from slop-rdf's vocab; a missing term goes upstream" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/d03dea42-7083-461f-833a-5acca0c08843> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/d03dea42-7083-461f-833a-5acca0c08843> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "HOWL names RDF, RDFS, OWL, XSD and SWRL terms only through slop-rdf's `vocab` constants, never string literals or local `const`s. `is-reserved-iri` (decode.slop) spelled out five namespace IRIs while `vocab` already exported `RDF_NS`, `RDFS_NS`, `OWL_NS` and `XSD_NS`; the user flagged it on 2026-09-30.\n\nowl2.slop carried 14 local constants, the SWRL namespace plus 13 terms, under an M0 note: \"an upstream PR is owed\". Nobody acted on the note until the user asked. slop-rdf PR #10 (merged 2026-09-30) added the OWL 2 reserved vocabulary slop-rdf lacked, plus the SWRL terms. owl2's local constants are gone, and decode and owl2 import from `vocab`.\n\n**Rule:**\n- Any IRI outside `@example` data and tests comes from `vocab`.\n- If `vocab` lacks the term, open the slop-rdf PR in the same change. A local constant is at most a bridge, and it names the PR.\n- An \"upstream PR is owed\" note is a task, not a comment: file it when written." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/d03dea42-7083-461f-833a-5acca0c08843> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/d03dea42-7083-461f-833a-5acca0c08843> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-09-30T20:55:38.301298Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/d03dea42-7083-461f-833a-5acca0c08843> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "IRIs come from slop-rdf's vocab; a missing term goes upstream" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/d03dea42-7083-461f-833a-5acca0c08843> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#learnedFrom> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/8c12dc86-3434-47e9-ab7d-3dd12d828cbe> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/d0470196-ffc3-4de7-8bb8-4c5564a029e5> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Lesson> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/d0470196-ffc3-4de7-8bb8-4c5564a029e5> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "SLOP drops multi-payload pattern bindings in expression-position match" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/d0470196-ffc3-4de7-8bb8-4c5564a029e5> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/d0470196-ffc3-4de7-8bb8-4c5564a029e5> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "A `match` arm destructuring a multi-payload union variant — e.g. `(sub-some-rhs c rr d)` over NormAxiom — compiles correctly in STATEMENT position but not when the `match` is lowered as an expression (for instance nested inside an `and` operand). There the transpiler emits `__auto_type c = _mv.data.sub_some_rhs;`, binding the FIRST name to the whole payload struct and never declaring `rr` or `d`. The SLOP checker accepts it; cc then fails with \"use of undeclared identifier 'rr'\" and a struct-to-types_Node type mismatch. In statement position the same arm lowers to `.f0 / .f1 / .f2` field bindings.\n\nEvidence: src/test.slop test-range-complex-fillers-stay-apart, 2026-09-14. The inlined form failed at csrc/src/slop_test.c:1452; moving the same match into its own function (complex-range-fillers-distinct), whose body is a let/do in statement position, compiled and passed. The existing test-range-elimination-introduces-a-shared-filler uses the identical pattern in statement position and always compiled.\n\nRule: never destructure a multi-payload variant inside a `match` that is itself an operand of `and`/`or` or another expression. Put that match in a helper function (statement position) and combine the helper's Bool result. A cc \"undeclared identifier\" naming a pattern variable is this bug, not a typo. Distinct from the existing Lesson that multi-payload variants COMPARE only their first payload — that one is about generated equality, this one about pattern binding." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/d0470196-ffc3-4de7-8bb8-4c5564a029e5> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/d0470196-ffc3-4de7-8bb8-4c5564a029e5> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-09-14T22:46:36.392614Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/d0470196-ffc3-4de7-8bb8-4c5564a029e5> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "SLOP drops multi-payload pattern bindings in expression-position match" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/e1ae09a0-af91-46db-bdb1-88fb030285ce> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Lesson> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/e1ae09a0-af91-46db-bdb1-88fb030285ce> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "slop boundary additions found building el++'s rules (main 28a6270)" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/e1ae09a0-af91-46db-bdb1-88fb030285ce> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/e1ae09a0-af91-46db-bdb1-88fb030285ce> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Writing el++'s rule contracts and engine on slop main 28a6270 found seven boundaries not in the earlier boundary Lessons. Each was isolated by a minimal probe, and each has a workaround in the tree.\n\nVERIFIER:\n1. A nested single-payload `union-new` (e.g. `(union-new KTerm k-name z)` inside a head), or one returned directly, does not have its payload modelled. A helper call that body and contract both make compares, because it is the same uninterpreted term.\n2. `(not (. $result flag))` does not translate; `(== (. $result flag) false)` does.\n3. A field projected from a call's record result, `(. (f q) fires)`, in a @loop-invariant or @post is not linked to the same call in the body. Matching on an Option-returning call is linked.\n4. A for-each element is only \"some member of the list\". No invariant can say \"every element so far\", so a filter's completeness (`forall q in ps: … list-contains $result …`) is REFUTED, not unknown, even over Int elements.\n5. A bare Bool field as a filter loop's `when` test crashes the verifier: a Z3 sort mismatch in _extract_seq_push_axioms, which reads the field as Int. `(== (. c fires) true)` avoids it.\n\nTOOLCHAIN:\n6. `@example :eq f` applies only to list results. A record result is compared with C `==`, which does not compile.\n7. A `(list T …)` literal returned from a function is emitted as a C compound literal in the callee's stack frame, so the caller gets a dangling array. It segfaulted at -O2 and was silent under ASan (stack-use-after-return detection is off). Use a `match` on an index, or build the list in an arena.\n\nHow to apply: before concluding a contract is unprovable, try the shapes above, and probe a minimal pair in scratch first. Items 4, 5 and 7 are upstream defects worth reporting to slop." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/e1ae09a0-af91-46db-bdb1-88fb030285ce> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "superseded" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/e1ae09a0-af91-46db-bdb1-88fb030285ce> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-10-01T07:58:11.9846Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
