<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/e1ae09a0-af91-46db-bdb1-88fb030285ce> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#isSupersededBy> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/e7660360-15e3-4e73-8b84-af1ee2959d3a> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/e1ae09a0-af91-46db-bdb1-88fb030285ce> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#learnedFrom> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/4ee4d605-d01c-4259-89cf-e0b417e055ba> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/e1ae09a0-af91-46db-bdb1-88fb030285ce> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#learnedFrom> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/a3e2e732-fcf9-48b3-9f2c-ed2903975fc4> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/e7660360-15e3-4e73-8b84-af1ee2959d3a> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Lesson> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/e7660360-15e3-4e73-8b84-af1ee2959d3a> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "slop boundary additions found building el++'s rules (main 28a6270)" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/e7660360-15e3-4e73-8b84-af1ee2959d3a> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/e7660360-15e3-4e73-8b84-af1ee2959d3a> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Writing el++'s rule contracts and engine on slop main 28a6270 found seven verifier and toolchain boundaries, each isolated by a minimal probe. All were reported upstream. Status as of slop main 7380645:\n\n1. FIXED (#249): a nested single-payload `union-new`, or one returned directly, did not have its payload modelled.\n2. FIXED: `(not (. $result flag))` did not translate.\n3. FIXED (#251): a field projected from a pure call's record result was not linked between body and invariant.\n4. FIXED (#247): a for-each element was only \"some member of the list\", so a filter's completeness was REFUTED. `(list-visited xs)` in a @loop-invariant now names the visited prefix. Still limited: the source must be a parameter, not a local list.\n5. FIXED (#246, #250): a bare Bool field as a filter loop's `when` test crashed the verifier with a Z3 sort mismatch.\n6. FIXED (#252): `@example :eq f` applied only to list results.\n7. FIXED (#245): a `(list T …)` literal returned from a function was a dangling C compound literal in the callee's frame. It segfaulted at -O2 and was silent under ASan.\n\nAlso fixed in #248, found while prototyping #247: a trigger pattern on `field(seq.nth S i)` never fires, because Z3 rewrites seq.nth, so a proved invariant was useless as a hypothesis. And `list-contains` over a push-built list timed out step checks.\n\nStill true: where a contract can be stated in two shapes, prefer the one the solver can REFUTE when broken, not only prove when right. el++'s join states its invariants over an Option view for that reason (AD for the join combinator). How to apply: probe a minimal pair in scratch before concluding something is unprovable, and report a confirmed gap upstream with its repro." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/e7660360-15e3-4e73-8b84-af1ee2959d3a> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
