<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/ba8740d1-923c-4f65-83eb-925ea0a38683> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Rationale: A failed thread spawn is undetectable from SLOP until the thread module reports it" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/bbc89446-ab5c-4a9f-bc38-767331f3e725> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Rationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/bbc89446-ab5c-4a9f-bc38-767331f3e725> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Rationale: retract An empty slop List grows in the pushing function's arena, not the one it was made in" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/bbc89446-ab5c-4a9f-bc38-767331f3e725> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/bbc89446-ab5c-4a9f-bc38-767331f3e725> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "This lesson is no longer true since slop #278 (merged 2026-10-03, df93c3a). A list made by `list-new na` now grows in `na` wherever it is pushed, so the empty-List growth trap it describes cannot happen. `delta-push`, the workaround it recommended, is removed. The current rule and the cross-thread `:arena` case are in Lesson c75e8926, which superseded 6245f8b5. The historical fact it recorded is kept in Consequence 982f9d9e: about 0.9 GB leaked on EL-GALEN before slice 6b part 2." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/bbc89446-ab5c-4a9f-bc38-767331f3e725> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/bbc89446-ab5c-4a9f-bc38-767331f3e725> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-10-03T16:57:41.767849Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/bbc89446-ab5c-4a9f-bc38-767331f3e725> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Rationale: retract An empty slop List grows in the pushing function's arena, not the one it was made in" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/c7778c70-10ba-4027-a17a-ce6f54b3e0ec> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Rationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/c7778c70-10ba-4027-a17a-ce6f54b3e0ec> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Rationale: retract Serve CR4's on-edge trigger from a by-role bucket (∃r.B ⊑ A filed under r, then test B ∈ S(Y)) — rejected: one role such as part_of heads thousands of such axioms while a context holds tens of subsumers, so walking S(Y) is the cheaper side." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/c7778c70-10ba-4027-a17a-ce6f54b3e0ec> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/c7778c70-10ba-4027-a17a-ce6f54b3e0ec> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Its reasoning, that walking S(Y) is always CR4's cheaper side, was disproved by the S6b profile: on EL-GALEN the S(Y) walk cost 27.8M rule calls for 579k conclusions. M1 slice 6b step A walks whichever side is smaller. The replacement is Alternative 76992b94, weighed by AD 3e6b52c2, which is linked here by `supersedes`." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/c7778c70-10ba-4027-a17a-ce6f54b3e0ec> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/c7778c70-10ba-4027-a17a-ce6f54b3e0ec> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-09-28T17:19:24.466076Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/c7778c70-10ba-4027-a17a-ce6f54b3e0ec> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Rationale: retract Serve CR4's on-edge trigger from a by-role bucket (∃r.B ⊑ A filed under r, then test B ∈ S(Y)) — rejected: one role such as part_of heads thousands of such axioms while a context holds tens of subsumers, so walking S(Y) is the cheaper side." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/d610f69d-12fa-4e06-801b-05b3c4efa76f> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Rationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/d610f69d-12fa-4e06-801b-05b3c4efa76f> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "record-was-inaccurate" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/d610f69d-12fa-4e06-801b-05b3c4efa76f> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Rationale: Range-bearing inputs gate only on HermiT; ELK's range results are informational" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/d610f69d-12fa-4e06-801b-05b3c4efa76f> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/d610f69d-12fa-4e06-801b-05b3c4efa76f> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "The superseded record's consequence said census cannot see owl:AllDisjointClasses. The probe label check added after the Codex review caught this, and census now counts it as DisjointClasses. Routing also gained a guard that the superseded record lacked: input that sits in an OWL API blind spot is not diffed against either oracle." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/d610f69d-12fa-4e06-801b-05b3c4efa76f> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/d610f69d-12fa-4e06-801b-05b3c4efa76f> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-09-27T03:01:22.035441Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/d610f69d-12fa-4e06-801b-05b3c4efa76f> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Rationale: Range-bearing inputs gate only on HermiT; ELK's range results are informational" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
